; wm.l0 -- the compositor: owns the screen, through the display protocol
; (display.l0), and keeps windows on it for its clients (wm.l0's
; protocol). It never copies a window's pixels: each client draws into a
; buffer it shares, and wm stacks the buffers into the screen as layers,
; which the display driver composes. Its own buffers are the desktop, the
; pointer's image, the top bar, and each window's chrome: its title bar,
; and under its content a frame, a thin border down the content's sides
; and along its foot, in the title bar's color.
;
; The top bar is GNOME Shell's, across the top of the screen and over
; the windows: Applications, which opens the launcher (launcher.l0), a
; page of every app's icon, which a click starts; the name of the front
; window's app, from its bundle's manifest (app.l0), or its title; and the
; date and time, which the clock (rtc clock) tells wm at the start of
; every minute.
;
; Keys go to the window in front. A press of the pointer's left button
; on a window brings it to the front; on its title bar it starts a drag,
; which moves it while the button is held; on an edge of it, or the
; border just outside, it starts a resize: the client is asked for the
; size the pointer's drag gives (size_notice), and answers with a new
; buffer (the resize request), which replaces the old one. draw's commands
; paint the desktop, behind the windows.
;
; A title bar is an Adwaita header bar, laid out and painted by the
; toolkit (user/lib/ui): the title in bold in its middle, and a round
; close button at its end; lighter, its title dimmed, in the backdrop,
; when its window is not in front. The pointer is Adwaita's arrow. A
; client may decorate its window itself (the csd request), as GNOME's own
; apps do: wm then draws no title bar or frame for it, the whole window is
; its content, all four corners rounded, the border round it resizes it,
; and its client asks wm to move it (move) when its own header bar is
; dragged.
;
; On a large screen the display says the scale is 2 (display.l0): wm then
; lays everything out in the desktop's pixels, half the screen's each
; way, and its buffers and its clients' are twice as wide and high,
; painted at the screen's own resolution with the face for scale 2
; (face.l0). Everything here, the windows, the pointer, the protocol's
; numbers, is the desktop's pixels; display.l0 makes them the screen's.
;
; The pointer goes to clients as Wayland's does: each move and press in a
; window's content to that window, relative to it; after a press, to the
; same window until every button is up, wherever the pointer goes; and a
; leave notice when it goes from a window. The scroll wheel's turns go
; to the window the pointer would, relative to it, as WheelEvents. A
; window coming to the front, and going from it, is told with a focus
; notice (l0s.l0). Every notice to a client names its window, as
; Wayland's events name their surface: it goes as a window notice,
; "win" and the window's id before it (l0s.l0's win_notice), a driver's
; key passed on as it came after them, so a client may give all its
; windows one port.

(def title_h () int (ui_headerbar_h))
; How bright the wallpaper is drawn: as bright as the display drivers
; show it before wm starts, so that nothing changes under the desktop
; as it comes.
(def wallpaper_percent () int 100)

; The wallpaper at scale s (render.l0's wallpaper_load): the image the
; display driver showed first.
(def load_wallpaper ((s int) (percent int)) BgLoad (wallpaper_load s percent))

; The desktop's buffer is 0, the pointer's 1, the top bar's 2, the
; launcher's 3, the menu's card's menu_id, and window i's content and chrome 4 + 4i + 2k and
; 5 + 4i + 2k, k its bank, 0 or 1. A resize makes the window's new
; buffers in the other bank, shows them, and then forgets the old ones:
; the display refuses to forget a buffer on the screen, and one made
; again under its id would leave its old pages mapped.
(def desktop_id () int 0)
(def arrow_id () int 1)
(def bar_id () int 2)
(def launcher_id () int 3)

; The menu's card, over the windows and under the bar. Windows' buffers
; count up from 4, so its id is well past any of them.
(def menu_id () int 100000)
(def content_id ((i int) (k int)) int (add 4 (add (mul 4 i) (mul 2 k))))
(def chrome_id ((i int) (k int)) int (add 5 (add (mul 4 i) (mul 2 k))))

; During a drag, rebuild the screen once 20 ms have passed since the last
; rebuild ended: rebuilding costs more than a move, so the moves in
; between only move the window, and the next rebuild shows the latest.
(def drag_ns () int 20000000)

; -------------------------------------------------------------- windows

; A window: its id, the port its events go to, its client's pid, its top
; left, its content's width and height, the row its buffer is read from,
; its title, the canvas of its chrome, where in wm its content's and its
; chrome's buffers are, to give them up when it closes, how many pages
; they are and where the display has them, the name of the app its client
; is, "" if it is none, how it is being resized, and who draws its title
; bar. A window whose client draws its own has no chrome: its canvas is
; empty, and it has no chrome's buffer.
(data Win (Win int int int int int int int int (list int) Canvas int int Bufs (list int) Sizing Deco))

; Who decorates a window: wm, with a title bar and a frame, as the
; window request asks; or its client, which draws its own header bar in
; its content, as the csd request asks, xdg-decoration's client side.
(data Deco (ServerSide) (ClientSide))

; How many rows of a window's top are wm's title bar, and how thick its
; frame is: none of either for a window its client decorates.
(def bar_rows ((dc Deco)) int (match dc ((ServerSide) (title_h)) ((ClientSide) 0)))
(def border ((dc Deco)) int (match dc ((ServerSide) (edge)) ((ClientSide) 0)))

; Whether wm draws a window's title bar and frame.
(def has_chrome ((dc Deco)) bool (match dc ((ServerSide) true) ((ClientSide) false)))

; A window's buffers as shared: how many pages its content is, as its
; client shared them, where the display has them, and how many of its own
; pixels apart its rows are; and its chrome's pages and where the display
; has them, its rows as far apart as its canvas is wide. Each may be more
; than its size takes, room to grow into, so that a resize to a size that
; fits is shown in the same pages, every row where it was: no page is
; shared or given up, which is what costs most, and what the client had
; painted stays put for it to paint only what changed. Then whether its
; client has asked to be told the next frame (frame ID); the bank of the
; content's id, which a resize flips with the chrome's and an attach
; alone; and the content's other buffer, once its client has attached
; one: the one it paints while this one shows.
(data Bufs (Bufs int int int int int bool int Spare))

; A window's other buffer, its client's as attach gave it, under the
; content's other bank's id in the display: where it is in wm, its
; pages, where the display has them, how many of its own pixels apart its
; rows are, the size it was given the display at, the desktop's pixels,
; and whether it is attached, to show at the next damage; or none.
(data Spare (Spare int int int int int int bool) (NoSpare))

; The bank of w's content's id.
(def win_cbank ((w Win)) int
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (match bf ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp) ck)))))

; w's other buffer.
(def win_spare ((w Win)) Spare
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (match bf ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp) sp)))))

; The display's id for w's content, and for its other buffer.
(def win_content_id ((w Win)) int (content_id (win_id w) (win_cbank w)))
(def win_spare_id ((w Win)) int (content_id (win_id w) (sub 1 (win_cbank w))))

; Whether w's other buffer is attached, to show at the next damage.
(def win_pending ((w Win)) bool (match (win_spare w) ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend) pend) ((NoSpare) false)))

; How a window is resized: the bank its buffers' ids are in, the edges the
; user last dragged (the bits edge_left, edge_right, edge_top and
; edge_bottom, which say which sides stay and which move), the size last
; asked of its client, and whether an answer is awaited; then, while it
; is maximized, the place and size it is restored to, and while a
; maximize or a restore awaits the client's answer, the place and size it
; goes to; rect_none for none of either.
(data Sizing (Sizing int int int int bool Rect Rect))

; The bits of a window's edges: the left, the right, the top, the bottom.
(def edge_left () int 1)
(def edge_right () int 2)
(def edge_top () int 4)
(def edge_bottom () int 8)

; Whether the edges e include edge b.
(def has_edge ((e int) (b int)) bool (not (eq (bit_and e b) 0)))

; The bank of buffer ids a window's buffers are in.
(def sz_bank ((sz Sizing)) int (match sz ((Sizing k e ww wh asking re go) k)))

; Where window w is restored to, rect_none if it is not maximized.
(def win_restore ((w Win)) Rect
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
    (match sz ((Sizing k e ww wh asking re go) re)))))

; w with re to be restored to, and go the place and size it goes to once
; its client answers.
(def win_maxing ((w Win) (re Rect) (go Rect)) Win
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
    (match sz ((Sizing k e ww wh asking ore ogo) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app (Sizing k e ww wh asking re go) dc))))))

; The bank of buffer ids w's buffers are in.
(def win_bank ((w Win)) int
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (sz_bank sz))))

; w with its size asked for, as the pointer's drag wants it.
(def win_asked ((w Win) (edges int) (ww int) (wh int) (asking bool)) Win
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
    (match sz ((Sizing k e ow oh oa re go) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app (Sizing k edges ww wh asking re go) dc))))))

(def win_id ((w Win)) int (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) id)))
(def win_port ((w Win)) int (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) port)))
(def win_pid ((w Win)) int (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) pid)))

; Who decorates a window.
(def win_deco ((w Win)) Deco (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) dc)))

; A window's title.
(def win_title((w Win)) (list int) (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) title)))

(def win_at ((w Win) (x int) (y int)) Win
  (match w ((Win id port pid ox oy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc))))

(def win_top ((w Win) (top int)) Win
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch old title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc))))

(def win_titled ((w Win) (title (list int))) Win
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top old tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc))))

; A window's frame: a border edge pixels thick down its content's sides
; and along its foot, in its title bar's color, so the content sits in
; the title bar's ground. The frame is the part of the window's chrome
; under the title bar, a buffer as big as the whole window under the
; content, which covers all of it but the border and the corners its
; shape cuts.
(def edge () int 2)

; How wide a window decorated as dc is, its content cw wide; how high its
; frame is, its content ch high; and how high the whole window is, the
; title bar and the frame: for one its client decorates, its content's
; size.
(def outer_w ((dc Deco) (cw int)) int (add cw (mul 2 (border dc))))
(def frame_h ((dc Deco) (ch int)) int (add ch (border dc)))
(def chrome_h ((dc Deco) (ch int)) int (add (bar_rows dc) (frame_h dc ch)))

; The layers of windows, front first, as the display takes them: the
; desktop, then each window from the back, its chrome, and its content
; in its frame, then the top bar over them all. While the launcher is shown it is there instead of the
; windows, under the bar: they are hidden, and so the screen is rebuilt
; from fewer layers.
(def layers ((ws (list Win)) (shown bool)) (list Placed)
  (let top (cons (Placed (bar_id) 0 0 0) (nil Placed))
    (cons (Placed (desktop_id) 0 0 0)
          (if shown (cons (Placed (launcher_id) 0 (bar_h) 0) top) (window_layers ws top)))))

; ws, front first, consed onto acc a window at a time, so the front one's
; layers come last, on top: its chrome, if wm decorates it, and its
; content.
(def window_layers ((ws (list Win)) (acc (list Placed))) (list Placed)
  (if (is_empty ws)
      acc
      (match (head ws)
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (let content (cons (Placed (win_content_id (head ws)) (add x (border dc)) (add y (bar_rows dc)) top) acc)
            (window_layers (tail ws)
                           (if (has_chrome dc) (cons (Placed (chrome_id id (win_bank (head ws))) x y 0) content) content)))))))

; A title bar cw wide, as the toolkit lays it out: in front or not.
(def title_nodes ((title (list int)) (cw int) (front bool)) (list UiNode)
  (let st (ui_st_backdropped (ui_state_new (ui_style)) (not front))
    (ui_layout (UiHeaderBar (nil UiWidget) title
                            (cons (UiButton "win.close" "window-close" "" (UiBtnTitle) true) (nil UiWidget)))
               (Rect 0 0 cw (title_h)) st (ui_headerbar_bg (ui_style) front))))

; Whether x, y in a title bar cw wide is on its close button.
(def on_close ((cw int) (x int) (y int)) bool
  (eq (ui_hit (title_nodes "" cw true) x y) "win.close"))

; Where a press at x, y lands: on a window's close button, title bar,
; content or frame, or on an edge of it that resizes it (the edges as
; edges_at says), the frontmost there; or the desktop.
(data Hit (OnClose Win) (OnTitle Win) (OnContent Win int int) (OnFrame Win) (OnEdge Win int) (OnDesktop))

(def hit ((ws (list Win)) (x int) (y int)) Hit
  (if (is_empty ws)
      (OnDesktop)
      (match (head ws)
        ((Win id port pid wx wy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (let e (edges_at dc cw ch (sub x wx) (sub y wy))
            (if (not (eq e 0))
                (OnEdge (head ws) e)
                (if (in_window dc cw ch (sub x wx) (sub y wy))
                    (hit_in (head ws) dc cw ch (sub x wx) (sub y wy))
                    (hit (tail ws) x y))))))))

; How far outside a window its edges are still grabbed.
(def resize_border () int 6)

; The smallest a window's content is dragged to.
(def min_w () int 200)
(def min_h () int 100)

; How far along each side from a window's corner the corner is grabbed:
; both the edges that meet there.
(def resize_corner () int 20)

; The edges of a window, its content cw by ch, that x, y from its top left
; grabs, as edge_left and the others added together, or 0. Within
; resize_corner of a corner, the two edges that meet there, wherever
; nothing of the window's own is pressed (free_at): the border outside,
; the corners its shape cuts away, the frame, and the content's corners,
; cut to show the frame. Elsewhere one edge: the frame's sides and foot,
; and the border outside, resize_border wide; a window's top is its title
; bar, so only the border above it is an edge. A window its client
; decorates has no frame: the border outside it, all round, is its edges.
(def edges_at ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (x int) (y int)) int
  (let ow (outer_w dc cw)
    (let oh (chrome_h dc ch)
      (let b (resize_border)
        (if (if (if (lt x (sub 0 b)) true (ge x (add ow b))) true (if (lt y (sub 0 b)) true (ge y (add oh b))))
            0
            (let c (if (free_at dc cw ch x y) (corner_of ow oh x y) 0)
              (if (not (eq c 0)) c (side_edges dc ow oh x y))))))))

; The one edge, or none, x, y from the top left of a window ow by oh,
; decorated as dc, is on, as edges_at says.
(def side_edges ((dc Deco) (ow int) (oh int) (x int) (y int)) int
  (let e (border dc)
    (let t (bar_rows dc)
      (add (if (if (lt x 0) true (if (lt x e) (ge y t) false)) (edge_left) 0)
      (add (if (if (ge x ow) true (if (ge x (sub ow e)) (ge y t) false)) (edge_right) 0)
      (add (if (lt y 0) (edge_top) 0)
           (if (ge y (sub oh e)) (edge_bottom) 0)))))))

; The edges of the corner of a window ow by oh that x, y from its top left
; is within resize_corner of, both ways; 0 if none.
(def corner_of ((ow int) (oh int) (x int) (y int)) int
  (let hz (if (lt x (resize_corner)) (edge_left) (if (ge x (sub ow (resize_corner))) (edge_right) 0))
    (let vt (if (lt y (resize_corner)) (edge_top) (if (ge y (sub oh (resize_corner))) (edge_bottom) 0))
      (if (if (eq hz 0) true (eq vt 0)) 0 (add hz vt)))))

; Whether x, y from the top left of a window, its content cw by ch, is on
; nothing of the window's own to press: outside it, in a corner its shape
; cuts away, on its frame, or in a corner of its content, cut away to
; show the frame.
(def free_at ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (x int) (y int)) bool
  (if (not (if (if (ge x 0) (lt x (outer_w dc cw)) false) (if (ge y 0) (lt y (chrome_h dc ch)) false) false))
      true
      (if (cut_off dc cw ch x y)
          true
          (if (lt y (bar_rows dc))
              false
              (let cx (sub x (border dc))
                (let cy (sub y (bar_rows dc))
                  (if (if (if (ge cx 0) (lt cx cw) false) (lt cy ch) false)
                      (content_cut dc cw ch cx cy)
                      true)))))))

; Whether cx, cy in a content cw by ch is in one of its bottom corners,
; which the display cuts.
(def content_cut ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (cx int) (cy int)) bool
  (let inset (corner_cut (inner_radius dc cw ch) (sub (sub ch 1) cy))
    (if (lt cx inset) true (ge cx (sub cw inset)))))

; A window's content size.
(data Size (Size int int))

; The size a window, its content cw by ch at wx, wy, is dragged to by its
; edges e when the pointer has moved dx, dy: the edge on the side moved
; grows it, the opposite side stays; at least min_w by min_h, and no more
; than fits the desktop w by h below the top bar, decorated as dc.
(def resize_geometry ((dc Deco) (e int) (dx int) (dy int) (wx int) (wy int) (cw int) (ch int) (w int) (h int)) Size
  (Size (clamped (if (has_edge e (edge_left)) (sub cw dx) (if (has_edge e (edge_right)) (add cw dx) cw))
                (min_w)
                (if (has_edge e (edge_left)) (add wx cw) (sub (sub w wx) (mul 2 (border dc)))))
        (clamped (if (has_edge e (edge_top)) (sub ch dy) (if (has_edge e (edge_bottom)) (add ch dy) ch))
                 (min_h)
                 (if (has_edge e (edge_top))
                     (sub (add wy ch) (bar_h))
                     (sub (sub (sub h wy) (bar_rows dc)) (border dc))))))

; n kept from lo up to hi, or lo if there is no room.
(def clamped ((n int) (lo int) (hi int)) int (max lo (min n hi)))

; Whether x, y from a window's top left is on it, its content cw by ch:
; within its title bar and frame, and not in a corner cut away.
(def in_window ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (x int) (y int)) bool
  (if (if (ge x 0) (lt x (outer_w dc cw)) false)
      (if (if (ge y 0) (lt y (chrome_h dc ch)) false) (not (cut_off dc cw ch x y)) false)
      false))

; What x, y from the top left of window w, its content cw by ch, is on:
; all of a window its client decorates is its content.
(def hit_in ((w Win) (dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (x int) (y int)) Hit
  (if (lt y (bar_rows dc))
      (if (on_close (outer_w dc cw) x y) (OnClose w) (OnTitle w))
      (let cx (sub x (border dc))
        (let cy (sub y (bar_rows dc))
          (if (if (if (ge cx 0) (lt cx cw) false) (lt cy ch) false)
              (OnContent w cx cy)
              (OnFrame w))))))

; A window's rounded corners, Adwaita's 12: the title bar's top two, the
; frame's bottom two, each at most half of its buffer's sides; and the
; content's, inside the frame's by the border. A window its client
; decorates is its content alone, all four of its corners 12.
(def top_radius ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int)) int
  (min (ui_window_radius) (min (div (outer_w dc cw) 2) (div (match dc ((ServerSide) (title_h)) ((ClientSide) ch)) 2))))
(def bottom_radius ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int)) int (min (ui_window_radius) (min (div (outer_w dc cw) 2) (div (frame_h dc ch) 2))))
(def inner_radius ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int)) int (max 0 (sub (bottom_radius dc cw ch) (border dc))))

; Whether x, y from the top left of a window, its content cw by ch, is in
; a corner the display cuts away, and so shows what is under the window.
(def cut_off ((dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (x int) (y int)) bool
  (let rows (chrome_h dc ch)
    (let inset (max (corner_cut (top_radius dc cw ch) y) (corner_cut (bottom_radius dc cw ch) (sub (sub rows 1) y)))
      (if (lt x inset) true (ge x (sub (outer_w dc cw) inset))))))

; ws with window id first, the rest in order.
(def raised ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) (list Win)
  (match (find_win ws id)
    ((None) ws)
    ((Some w) (cons w (without_win ws id)))))

(def find_win ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) (Option Win)
  (if (is_empty ws) ((None Win)) (if (eq (win_id (head ws)) id) (Some (head ws)) (find_win (tail ws) id))))

(def without_win ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) (list Win)
  (if (is_empty ws) ws (if (eq (win_id (head ws)) id) (without_win (tail ws) id) (cons (head ws) (without_win (tail ws) id)))))

(def replaced ((ws (list Win)) (w Win)) (list Win)
  (if (is_empty ws) ws (if (eq (win_id (head ws)) (win_id w)) (cons w (tail ws)) (cons (head ws) (replaced (tail ws) w)))))

; The windows of pid.
(def of_pid ((ws (list Win)) (pid int)) (list Win)
  (if (is_empty ws) ws (if (eq (win_pid (head ws)) pid) (cons (head ws) (of_pid (tail ws) pid)) (of_pid (tail ws) pid))))

; Where the n-th window opens: down and right of the one before, back to
; the top left before it would leave a screen w by h.
(def cascade ((n int) (dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int) (w int) (h int)) Placed
  (let step (mod n 8)
    (let x (add 40 (mul step 60))
      (let y (add 40 (mul step 50))
        (Placed 0 (if (gt (add x (outer_w dc cw)) w) 40 x) (if (gt (add y (chrome_h dc ch)) h) 40 y) 0)))))

; The pointer's x or y, 0 to pointer_max, on a screen n pixels across.
(def scaled ((v int) (n int)) int (div (mul v (sub n 1)) (pointer_max)))

; ------------------------------------------------------------ the top bar

; GNOME Shell's top bar: black, across the top of the screen, over every
; window. At its start Applications, which opens the launcher, then the
; name of the front window's app, as GNOME Shell's app menu shows it, or
; its title if it is no app's; and the date and time, bold, in its
; middle. Windows open below it, and are never dragged under it, so a
; press on it is never a window's.
(def bar_h () int 32)
(def bar_bg () int (ui_black))
(def bar_fg () int (ui_white))

; The bar's canvas, the clock's pid, and the time it last said, each -1
; for none: with no clock running, the bar shows no time. Then the apps
; there are, which the launcher shows, the launcher, the L0S menu, and
; the launches wm waits on (launching.l0).
(data Bar (Bar Canvas int int (list App) Launcher Menu (list Launch)))

; The launches the bar waits on, and the bar with others.
(def bar_launches ((b Bar)) (list Launch) (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l m ls) ls)))
(def bar_waiting ((b Bar) (ls (list Launch))) Bar (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l m old) (Bar c cp t apps l m ls))))

; The clock's pid, the apps, the launcher, and the bar with another
; launcher.
(def bar_clock ((b Bar)) int (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l m ls) cp)))
(def bar_apps ((b Bar)) (list App) (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l m ls) apps)))
(def bar_launcher ((b Bar)) Launcher (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l m ls) l)))
(def bar_launched ((b Bar) (l Launcher)) Bar (match b ((Bar c cp t apps old m ls)(Bar c cp t apps l m ls))))

; The bar's menu, and the bar with another.
(def bar_menu ((b Bar)) Menu (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l m ls) m)))
(def bar_menued ((b Bar) (m Menu)) Bar (match b ((Bar c cp t apps l old ls)(Bar c cp t apps l m ls))))

; b with apps in place of the apps it had.
(def bar_with_apps ((b Bar) (apps (list App))) Bar (match b ((Bar c cp t old l m ls)(Bar c cp t apps l m ls))))

; Applications: its label, and how wide the bar's button for it is, 12
; either side. It starts after the logo's button, menu_logo_w in.
(def bar_apps_label () (list int) "Applications")
(def bar_apps_w () int (add (ui_text_w (bar_apps_label) (ui_text_font) false 1) (mul 2 (ui_space_m))))

; Where the bar's title starts: past the logo and Applications.
(def bar_title_x () int (add (menu_logo_w) (bar_apps_w)))

; The bar of a screen w wide, the launcher shown or not and the menu
; shown or not, showing title and clock: the logo, lit while the menu is
; open, Applications, lit while the launcher is open, then the title
; after it, cut short before it would reach the clock, 12 from it.
(def bar_ops ((w int) (shown bool) (menu bool) (title (list int)) (clock (list int))) (list UiPaint)
  (let lw (sub (sub (div (sub w (ui_text_w clock (ui_text_font) true 1)) 2) (ui_space_m)) (bar_title_x))
    (cons (UiPFill (Rect 0 0 w (bar_h)) (bar_bg))
      (bar_button_ops shown
        (cons (UiPText (Rect (bar_title_x) 0 (max 0 lw) (bar_h)) title (UiStart) (bar_fg) (ui_text_font) false 1)
          (cons (UiPText (Rect 0 0 w (bar_h)) clock (UiCenter) (bar_fg) (ui_text_font) true 1)
            (menu_button_ops menu (bar_h))))))))

; Applications onto ops: its label, on a pill while the launcher is open,
; 4 in from the button's edges.
(def bar_button_ops ((shown bool) (ops (list UiPaint))) (list UiPaint)
  (let x (menu_logo_w)
    (let label (UiPText (Rect x 0 (bar_apps_w) (bar_h)) (bar_apps_label) (UiCenter) (bar_fg) (ui_text_font) false 1)
      (if shown
          (cons (UiPRound (Rect (add x 4) 4 (sub (bar_apps_w) 8) (sub (bar_h) 8)) (div (sub (bar_h) 8) 2) (ui_bar_active_bg) (bar_bg))
                (cons label ops))
          (cons label ops)))))

; What the bar names: the front window's app, or its title; nothing while
; the launcher is shown.
(def bar_title ((ws (list Win)) (shown bool)) (list int)
  (if (if shown true (is_empty ws))
      ""
      (match (head ws) ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (if (is_empty app) title app)))))

(def bar_clock_text ((t int)) (list int) (if (lt t 0) "" (clock_text t)))

; The bar painted, for the windows and the time now, and shown.
(def draw_bar ((v Wm)) int
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match bar
        ((Bar c cp t apps l m ls)
          (let shown (launcher_shown l)
            (let p (ui_paint c font (Rect 0 0 w (bar_h)) (bar_ops w shown (menu_shown m) (bar_title ws shown) (bar_clock_text t)))
              (let e (display_damage d (bar_id) (Rect 0 0 w (bar_h))) 0))))))))

; The clock's notice that a minute has begun: the bar shows it.
(def ticked ((v Wm) (t int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match bar
        ((Bar c cp old apps l m ls)
          (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp (Bar c cp t apps l m ls))
            (let b (draw_bar v2) v2)))))))

; The name of the app pid is, from where its program is: "" if it is no
; app's, or has gone.
(def client_app ((bar Bar) (pid int)) (list int)
  (let path (proc_path pid)
    (if (is_empty path)
        ""
        (match (app_for_exec (bar_apps bar) path)
          ((None) (installed_app_name path))
          ((Some a) (app_name a))))))

; The name of the app whose program is at path, read from its bundle's
; manifest, for one the bar has not scanned yet: "" if it is no app's.
(def installed_app_name ((path (list int))) (list int)
  (match (app_for_path path)
    ((None) "")
    ((Some a) (app_name a))))

(def on_bar ((y int)) bool (lt y (bar_h)))

; Whether x, y is on the bar's Applications.
(def on_apps_button ((x int) (y int)) bool
  (if (on_bar y) (if (ge x (menu_logo_w)) (lt x (bar_title_x)) false) false))

; Whether x, y is on the bar's logo, the menu's button.
(def on_logo_button ((x int) (y int)) bool (if (on_bar y) (lt x (menu_logo_w)) false))

; A window's top y, kept below the bar.
(def below_bar ((y int)) int (max y (bar_h)))

; -------------------------------------------------------------- the state

; The pointer: where it is, and its buttons; the window whose content it
; was last in, and the window a press in its content holds it for until
; every button is up, each -1 for none; and the canvas of its image, and
; which pointer that shows, as ui_paint_named_cursor names them; and the
; last press on a title bar, to tell a double click.
(data Ptr (Ptr int int int int int Canvas (list int) TitleClick))

; A press on a window's title bar: the window's id, and when, in
; clock_ns; the id -1 for none, or once it made a double click.
(data TitleClick (TitleClick int int))

; Whether a press on window id's title bar at t is the second of a double
; click after the press tc: on the same window, within the toolkit's
; ui_double_ns, as GTK's header bar tells one.
(def title_double ((tc TitleClick) (id int) (t int)) bool
  (match tc
    ((TitleClick last at) (if (eq last id) (lt (sub t at) (ui_double_ns)) false))))

; A drag: the window, where the pointer holds it, and when the screen
; was last rebuilt for it; or a window's edges dragged to resize it: its
; id, the edges, where the pointer was pressed, and the window's top
; left and content size then; or none.
(data Drag (Dragging int int int int) (Resizing int int int int int int int int) (NoDrag))

; The compositor: the display, the windows whose close it has asked of
; their clients, the desktop's size, the desktop's canvas, the face, at
; the display's scale, the wallpaper, the windows, front first, the next
; window's number, the pointer and its drag, the keyboard and pointer
; drivers' pids, which their events come from, and the top bar.
(data Wm (Wm Display (list Closing) int int Canvas UiFace Background (list Win) int Ptr Drag int int Bar))

; A close asked, as xdg_toplevel's close asks it: window id's client,
; pid, sent the close notice, and killed at t, on clock_ns, if the window
; is still open then.
(data Closing (Closing int int int))

; How long a client has to close a window its close button asked it to:
; 2 seconds.
(def close_wait_ns () int 2000000000)

; Fails, saying why.
(def complain ((why (list int))) int (fail_as "wm" why))

; What wm says once it serves compositor: the screen's size in its own
; pixels and its scale, how many apps the launcher has, and whether a
; clock tells it the time.
(def desktop_line ((w int) (h int) (s int) (apps int) (clock bool)) (list int)
  (append "the screen is " (append (digits (mul w s)) (append "x" (append (digits (mul h s))
    (append " at scale " (append (digits s) (append ", " (append (digits apps)
      (append (if (eq apps 1) " app" " apps") (append (if clock ", with a clock" ", with no clock")
        ", serving compositor")))))))))))

; The desktop_line of v, given the clock c found, said; 0.
(def desktop_said ((v Wm) (c Clocked)) int
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match c
        ((Clocked cp t)
          (info_as "wm" (desktop_line w h (display_scale d) (length (bar_apps bar)) (ge cp 0))))))))

; The screen, laid out as a desktop of its size over its scale.
(def wm () int
  (match (display_info (display_open))
    ((NoInfo why) (complain why))
    ((Info d di) (match di ((DisplayInfo w h cursor s) (with_desktop d (div w s) (div h s) (ui_face_pointers (ui_face_load s))))))))

; A buffer of wm's own given to the display as buffer id: its own pixels'
; size, its address and its pages.
(def give_buffer ((d Display) (id int) (c Canvas) (va int) (pages int)) (list int)
  (display_buffer d id (canvas_w c) (canvas_h c) va pages))

(def with_desktop ((d Display) (w int) (h int) (face UiFace)) int
  (match (ui_buffer_at w h (display_scale d))
    ((UiNoBuf why) (complain why))
    ((UiBuf va pages c)
      (let bg (match (load_wallpaper (display_scale d) (wallpaper_percent)) ((BgOk b) b) ((BgBad why) (NoBackground)))
        (let p (paint_background c bg)
          (let e (give_buffer d (desktop_id) c va pages)
            (if (not (is_empty e))
                (complain e)
                (with_arrow d w h c bg face))))))))

; The pointer's arrow: 64 by 64 of the screen's pixels at any scale, its
; hot spot its tip, Adwaita's, twice the size at scale 2.
(def with_arrow ((d Display) (w int) (h int) (desk Canvas) (bg Background) (face UiFace)) int
  (match (ui_buffer 64 64)
    ((UiNoBuf why) (complain why))
    ((UiBuf va pages c)
      (let a (ui_paint_cursor c face)
        (let e (give_buffer d (arrow_id) c va pages)
          (let e2 (display_cursor d (arrow_id) 0 0)
            (with_bar d w h desk bg face c)))))))

; The top bar: as wide as the screen, over everything but the pointer,
; whose image is ac.
(def with_bar ((d Display) (w int) (h int) (desk Canvas) (bg Background) (face UiFace) (ac Canvas)) int
  (match (ui_buffer_at w (bar_h) (display_scale d))
    ((UiNoBuf why) (complain why))
    ((UiBuf va pages c)
      (let e (give_buffer d (bar_id) c va pages)
        (let e2 (if (is_empty e) (display_layers d (layers (nil Win) false)) e)
          (if (not (is_empty e2))
              (complain e2)
              (listening (Wm d (nil Closing) w h desk face bg (nil Win) 0 (Ptr 0 0 0 -1 -1 ac "" (TitleClick -1 0)) (NoDrag) 0 0
                             (Bar c -1 -1 (app_bundles) (NoLauncher) (NoMenu) (nil Launch))))))))))

; Listens to the keyboard, the pointer and the clock, then serves
; compositor.
(def listening ((v Wm) ) int
  (let port (port_new)
    (let k (listen_pid_of (input_listen "keyboard" port))
      (let p (listen_pid_of (input_listen "pointer" port))
        (let c (clock_listen port k p)
          (let r (name_register_or_why port "compositor")
            (if (not (is_empty r))
                (complain r)
                (let fr (frames_listened v port)
                (let v2 (with_menu (with_launcher (with_drivers v k p c)))
                  (let n (desktop_said v2 c)
                    (let b (draw_bar v2)
                      (serve v2 port))))))))))))

; The display asked to tell port its frames and releases, which wm tells
; the windows' clients; a display that will not is said, and wm goes on
; without, its clients then told no frame: 0.
(def frames_listened ((v Wm) (port int)) int
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let e (display_frames d port)
        (if (is_empty e) 0 (warn_as "wm" (append "the display tells no frames: " e)))))))

; The clock's pid, and the time its reply gave; or -1 and -1, if no clock
; registers within clock_wait_ns.
(data Clocked (Clocked int int))

; A system with no clock waits only this long for one: rtc clock starts
; with the drivers, so is long registered when one is running.
(def clock_wait_ns () int 1000000000)

; The keyboard and the pointer are already telling port of their events,
; kp's and pp's, so those that come before the clock's reply are dropped:
; nothing else can send to port until it is registered.
(def clock_listen ((port int) (kp int) (pp int)) Clocked
  (match (name_wait "clock" (clock_wait_ns))
    ((NotFound) (Clocked -1 -1))
    ((Found c) (if (eq (port_send c (request port "listen")) (Sent)) (clock_reply port kp pp) (Clocked -1 -1)))))

(def clock_reply ((port int) (kp int) (pp int)) Clocked
  (match (port_receive port)
    ((RecvFailed) (Clocked -1 -1))
    ((Message from b)
      (if (if (eq from kp) true (eq from pp))
          (clock_reply port kp pp)
          (match (time_of (msg_text b))
            ((Some t) (Clocked from t))
            ((None) (Clocked -1 -1)))))))

(def with_drivers ((v Wm) (k int) (p int) (c Clocked)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag ok op bar)
      (match bar
        ((Bar bc ocp secs apps l m ls)
          (match c ((Clocked cp t) (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag k p (Bar bc cp t apps l m ls)))))))))

; --------------------------------------------------------------- serving

(def serve ((v Wm) (port int)) int
  (match (port_receive port)
    ((RecvFailed) (complain "lost its port"))
    ((Message from b) (took v port from b))))

; A message, its bytes b, from from, handled, then the next waited for. A
; mouse's motion is first joined by every motion queued behind it, so the
; pointer moves once for them all: each move waits for the display, a
; frame on the Pi 5's HVS, while a mouse reports every 8 ms or less, and
; moved one by one the pointer fell further and further behind.
(def took ((v Wm) (port int) (from int) (b bytes)) int
  (match (motion_from v from b)
    ((Some ev) (if (motion_joins ev) (gathered v port ev) (serve (received v port from b) port)))
    ((None) (serve (received v port from b) port))))

; ev, a motion, joined by each motion waiting on port that can be, then
; the pointer moved by them, and the first message that could not be
; joined handled.
(def gathered ((v Wm) (port int) (ev PointerMotion)) int
  (match (port_try_receive port)
    ((RecvFailed) (serve (nudged v ev) port))
    ((Message from b)
      (match (motion_from v from b)
        ((Some ev2) (if (motion_joins ev2) (if (same_buttons ev ev2) (gathered v port (motion_joined ev ev2)) (took (nudged v ev) port from b)) (took (nudged v ev) port from b)))
        ((None) (took (nudged v ev) port from b))))))

; The mouse's motion a message from from, its bytes b, is, if from is an
; input driver's and it is one. One driver may serve both the keyboard
; and the pointer, so the payload says what it is, not the pid.
(def motion_from ((v Wm) (from int) (b bytes)) (Option PointerMotion)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (if (from_input kp pp from) (pointer_motion_of (Message from b)) ((None PointerMotion))))))

; What a message is to wm's input: a key, the pointer's (a place, a
; motion or a wheel's turn), or neither, from no input driver.
(data InputKind (InputKey) (InputPointer) (NotInput))

; Whether from is the keyboard's driver, kp, or the pointer's, pp, each
; 0 until wm listens to it: possibly one process serving both.
(def from_input ((kp int) (pp int) (from int)) bool
  (if (gt from 0) (if (eq from kp) true (eq from pp)) false))

; What m, from from, is to wm's input, with kp and pp the keyboard's and
; the pointer's drivers: told apart by its payload, a key's notice or
; not, since both may come from one pid (usb-hid serves both).
(def input_kind ((kp int) (pp int) (m Message)) InputKind
  (match m
    ((RecvFailed) (NotInput))
    ((Message from b)
      (if (from_input kp pp from)
          (match (key_event_of m) ((Some k) (InputKey)) ((None) (InputPointer)))
          (NotInput)))))

; Whether a motion may join others: one that turns no wheel, since a
; turn goes where the pointer is when it comes.
(def motion_joins ((ev PointerMotion)) bool
  (match ev ((PointerMotion dx dy buttons wdx wdy) (if (eq wdx 0) (eq wdy 0) false))))

; Whether two motions hold the same buttons down, so no press or release
; is lost by joining them.
(def same_buttons ((a PointerMotion) (b PointerMotion)) bool
  (match a ((PointerMotion ax ay ab awx awy) (match b ((PointerMotion bx by bb bwx bwy) (eq ab bb))))))

; Two motions as one: their moves added.
(def motion_joined ((a PointerMotion) (b PointerMotion)) PointerMotion
  (match a ((PointerMotion ax ay ab awx awy) (match b ((PointerMotion bx by bb bwx bwy) (PointerMotion (add ax bx) (add ay by) bb 0 0))))))

; A message, its bytes b, from from: a key, the pointer, an exit, the
; time, or a request. Keys and the pointer are read in place, told apart
; by what they say (input_kind).
(def received ((v Wm) (port int) (from int) (b bytes)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (input_kind kp pp (Message from b))
        ((InputKey) (keyed v b))
        ((InputPointer) (pointer_received v (Message from b)))
        ((NotInput) (received_other v port from b))))))

; A message, its bytes b, from from, that is no input: an exit, the
; kernel's alarm, the time, the display's notice, or a request.
(def received_other ((v Wm) (port int) (from int) (b bytes)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (if (eq from 0)
          (if (is_alarm_notice (Message from b))
              (closes_due v port (clock_ns))
              (match (exit_of (Message from b))
                ((Exited pid status) (gone v pid))
                ((NotExit) v)))
          (if (eq from (bar_clock bar))
              (match (time_of (msg_text b))
                ((Some t) (ticked v t))
                ((None) v))
              (if (eq from (display_pid d))
                  (display_noticed v (Message from b))
                  (replied v port from (msg_text b))))))))

; What the pointer's driver sent: a tablet's place, a mouse's motion, or
; a wheel's turn.
(def pointer_received ((v Wm) (m Message)) Wm
  (match (pointer_event_of m)
    ((Some ev) (pointed v ev))
    ((None)
      (match (pointer_motion_of m)
        ((Some ev) (nudged v ev))
        ((None)
          (match (wheel_event_of m)
            ((Some ev) (wheeled v ev))
            ((None) v)))))))

; A key, its message's bytes b, to the window in front, passed on as it
; came; or the launcher's, while it is shown.
(def keyed ((v Wm) (b bytes)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (if (menu_shown (bar_menu bar))
          (menu_keyed v (key_event_of (Message kp b)))
          (if (launcher_shown (bar_launcher bar))
              (launcher_keyed v (key_event_of (Message kp b)))
              (match (key_window ws)
                ((None) v)
                ((Some kw) (let s (port_forward_win (win_port kw) (win_id kw) b) v))))))))

; The window a key goes to: the front one, of whichever client, whose id
; the key is told with; none with no window.
(def key_window ((ws (list Win))) (Option Win) (if (is_empty ws) ((None Win)) (Some (head ws))))

; A request answered; or an app's answer to an open wm asked of it,
; shown ID, which is no request (appopen.l0).
(def replied ((v Wm) (port int) (from int) (payload (list int))) Wm
  (match (app_shown_of payload)
    ((Some id) (launch_answer v from id))
    ((None)
      (let ws (split_spaces (request_body payload))
        (if (if (is_empty ws) false (eq (head ws) "resize"))
            (resize_replied v from payload (tail ws))
            (match (requested v port from ws)
              ((Served v2 reply) (let s (request_answer payload reply) v2))))))))

; hello's reply: who wm is, and the scale clients draw at.
(def hello_reply ((s int)) (list int) (append "compositor scale " (digits s)))

; The desktop's scale: how many of the screen's pixels each way one of
; its is.
(def wm_scale ((v Wm)) int (match v ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) (display_scale d))))

(def okay ((v Wm)) (Served Wm) (served_ok v))
(def refused ((v Wm) (why (list int))) (Served Wm) (served_error v why))

; A request's words answered: those of words, and those of numbers,
; whose first four are numbers, as server.l0's word_number reads them.
(def requested ((v Wm) (port int) (from int) (ws (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (if (is_empty ws)
      (refused v "no request")
      (let op (head ws)
        (let args (tail ws)
          (if (eq op "hello") (Served v (hello_reply (wm_scale v)))
          (if (eq op "windows") (Served v (window_lines v))
          (if (eq op "desktop") (drew v args)
          (if (eq op "title") (requested_title v args)
          (if (eq op "apps") (okay (apps_refreshed v))
          (if (eq op "end") (ended v from)
          (if (eq op "launch") (launch_requested v args)
          (match (word_numbers (take args 4))
            ((None) (refused v (append op "'s numbers are not numbers")))
            ((Some ns) (requested_window v from op ns args))))))))))))))

; title ID WORDS...: window ID's title made the words.
(def requested_title ((v Wm) (args (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (match (if (is_empty args) ((None int)) (word_number (head args)))
    ((None) (refused v "title takes an id"))
    ((Some id) (retitled v id (unwords (tail args))))))

; A request of a window, ns the numbers its first four arguments are.
(def requested_window ((v Wm) (from int) (op (list int)) (ns (list int)) (args (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (if (if (eq op "window") (ge (length args) 4) false) (window_came (opened v from ns (unwords (drop args 4)) (ServerSide)) from)
  (if (if (eq op "csd") (ge (length args) 4) false) (window_came (opened v from ns (unwords (drop args 4)) (ClientSide)) from)
  (if (eq op "damage") (requested_damage v args)
  (requested_of_one v from op ns args)))))

; A window or csd request served, s, for from: if it opened the window,
; a launch waiting on from's start is done (launch_window_came).
(def window_came ((s (Served Wm)) (from int)) (Served Wm)
  (match s
    ((Served v reply) (if (starts_with reply "window ") (Served (launch_window_came v from) reply) s))))

; The requests of one window by its id, and top's row.
(def requested_of_one ((v Wm) (from int) (op (list int)) (ns (list int)) (args (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (if (if (eq op "top") (eq (length args) 2) false) (topped v (nth ns 0) (nth ns 1))
  (if (if (eq op "frame") (eq (length args) 1) false) (frame_asked v from (nth ns 0))
  (if (if (eq op "attach") (eq (length args) 4) false) (attach_asked v from (nth ns 0) (nth ns 1) (nth ns 2) (nth ns 3))
  (if (if (eq op "close") (eq (length args) 1) false) (closed v (nth ns 0))
  (if (if (eq op "move") (eq (length args) 1) false) (move_started v from (nth ns 0))
  (if (if (eq op "maximize") (eq (length args) 1) false) (maximize_asked v from (nth ns 0))
  (if (if (eq op "edges") (eq (length args) 2) false) (edges_started v from (nth ns 0) (nth ns 1))
  (refused v (append "no request " op))))))))))

; damage ID X Y W H ...: each window's rectangle shown, five numbers each.
(def requested_damage ((v Wm) (args (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (match (if (if (gt (length args) 0) (eq (mod (length args) 5) 0) false) (word_numbers args) ((None (list int))))
    ((None) (refused v "no request damage"))
    ((Some ns) (damaged v ns (nil Dirty)))))

; ------------------------------------------------------------- requests

; window W H VA PORT TITLE, or csd with the same: a new window in front,
; decorated as dc.
(def opened ((v Wm) (from int) (ns (list int)) (title (list int)) (dc Deco)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let cw (nth ns 0)
        (let ch (nth ns 1)
          (if (if (lt cw 1) true (if (lt ch 1) true (gt (outer_w dc cw) w)))
              (refused v "a window must fit the screen")
              (match (display_buffer_shared d (content_id n 0) (mul cw (display_scale d)) (mul ch (display_scale d)) (mul cw (display_scale d))
                                            (nth ns 2) (content_pages cw ch (display_scale d)))
                ((Err e) (refused v e))
                ((Ok dcva) (titled_window v from (nth ns 3) cw ch (nth ns 2) dcva title dc)))))))))

; The pages of a client's content, cw by ch of the desktop's pixels, at
; scale s.
(def content_pages ((cw int) (ch int) (s int)) int (buffer_pages (mul cw s) (mul ch s)))

(def titled_window ((v Wm) (from int) (port int) (cw int) (ch int) (cva int) (dcva int) (title (list int)) (dc Deco)) (Served Wm)
  (match (watch_client v from)
    ((Watched) (if (has_chrome dc) (watched_window v from port cw ch cva dcva title) (watched_bare v from port cw ch cva dcva title)))
    ((WatchNoProc) (refused v "the client has gone"))
    ((WatchFull) (refused v "too many ports watch the client"))))

; Has from's exit, a client's, told to wm's port, so that its windows
; close when it does.
(def watch_client ((v Wm) (from int)) Watch
  (match (wm_port v)
    ((Found port) (proc_watch from port))
    ((NotFound) (WatchNoProc))))

; A window for from, whose exit is watched, its content at cva here and
; dcva in the display: its chrome made, and both its buffers shaped, the
; window's corners rounded (shape_window), then it is shown in front.
(def watched_window ((v Wm) (from int) (port int) (cw int) (ch int) (cva int) (dcva int) (title (list int))) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (ui_buffer_at (outer_w (ServerSide) cw) (chrome_h (ServerSide) ch) (display_scale d))
        ((UiNoBuf why) (refused v why))
        ((UiBuf tva pages tc)
          (match (display_buffer_shared d (chrome_id n 0) (canvas_w tc) (canvas_h tc) (canvas_w tc) tva pages)
            ((Err e) (let u (ui_buffer_free tva pages tc) (refused v e)))
            ((Ok dtva)
              (let s (shape_window d n 0 0 (ServerSide) cw ch)
                (match (cascade n (ServerSide) cw ch w h)
                  ((Placed z x y top)
                    (let bf (Bufs (content_pages cw ch (display_scale d)) dcva (mul cw (display_scale d)) pages dtva false 0 (NoSpare))
                      (let win (Win n port from x y cw ch 0 title tc cva tva bf (client_app bar from) (Sizing 0 0 cw ch false (rect_none) (rect_none)) (ServerSide))
                        (let f (refocused ws (cons win ws))
                          (shown_front (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (cons win ws) (add n 1) ptr drag kp pp bar) n))))))))))))))

; A window for from that its client decorates, its content at cva here
; and dcva in the display: no chrome, and its content's four corners
; rounded, then shown in front. Its chrome's canvas is empty, and its
; pages none.
(def watched_bare ((v Wm) (from int) (port int) (cw int) (ch int) (cva int) (dcva int) (title (list int))) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let s (shape_window d n 0 0 (ClientSide) cw ch)
        (match (cascade n (ClientSide) cw ch w h)
          ((Placed z x y top)
            (let bf (Bufs (content_pages cw ch (display_scale d)) dcva (mul cw (display_scale d)) 0 0 false 0 (NoSpare))
              (let win (Win n port from x y cw ch 0 title (canvas_new 0 0 0) cva 0 bf (client_app bar from) (Sizing 0 0 cw ch false (rect_none) (rect_none)) (ClientSide))
                (let f (refocused ws (cons win ws))
                  (shown_front (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (cons win ws) (add n 1) ptr drag kp pp bar) n))))))))))

; Window i's buffers shaped, its chrome in bank k and its content in bank
; kc, its content cw by ch, decorated as dc: the chrome's top corners as
; the title bar's, its bottom ones as the frame's, and the content's
; inside those; or, with no chrome, the content's four, as a window's.
(def shape_window ((d Display) (i int) (k int) (kc int) (dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int)) int
  (if (has_chrome dc)
      (let s1 (display_shape d (chrome_id i k) (top_radius dc cw ch) (top_radius dc cw ch) (bottom_radius dc cw ch) (bottom_radius dc cw ch))
        (shape_content d (content_id i kc) dc cw ch))
      (shape_content d (content_id i kc) dc cw ch)))

; A window's content, buffer id, its content cw by ch, decorated as dc,
; shaped as shape_window says.
(def shape_content ((d Display) (id int) (dc Deco) (cw int) (ch int)) int
  (if (has_chrome dc)
      (let s (display_shape d id 0 0 (inner_radius dc cw ch) (inner_radius dc cw ch)) 0)
      (let s (display_shape d id (top_radius dc cw ch) (top_radius dc cw ch) (bottom_radius dc cw ch) (bottom_radius dc cw ch)) 0)))

; resize ID W H [VA [N [S]]], from from, in payload: window ID's content
; made W by H, in the buffer it has, its rows where they were, or in a new
; one of N pages at VA, its rows S of its own pixels apart, with a chrome
; made to fit, all under the other bank of ids and shown at once;
; the old ids are forgotten, and any buffer no longer used given up. The
; window's top left moves with an edge dragged left or up, so that the
; opposite edge stays where it was. Refused, and the window as it was, if
; from is not its client, the size does not fit the screen or the
; buffer, or the display will not have the content.
;
; Each buffer the display has is given again in the same pages when the
; new size fits them, as a client that keeps room in its buffer does:
; only a buffer that must grow is shared anew, with room to grow more.
; It is answered as soon as the display has the new content, and the
; client asked then for the size the user has dragged to since, if that
; is another, so that the client paints it while wm makes the rest. If
; the rest cannot be made, the window stays as it was, and its client is
; asked for the size it shows.
(def resize_replied ((v Wm) (from int) (payload (list int)) (args (list (list int)))) Wm
  (match (if (if (ge (length args) 3) (le (length args) 6) false) (word_numbers args) ((None (list int))))
    ((None) (answered (refused v "no request resize") payload))
    ((Some ns)
      (match (resize_checked v from ns)
        ((Err why) (answered (refused v why) payload))
        ((Ok win) (resize_content v win (nth ns 1) (nth ns 2) (resize_where win ns (wm_scale v)) payload))))))

; Where a resize's content is in wm: its address, how many pages, 0 for
; as many as its size takes, and how many of its own pixels apart its
; rows are.
(data Where (Where int int int))

; Where a resize's numbers ns say the content is, at scale s: in the
; window's own buffer, with no VA; else at VA, in N pages, or as many as
; the size takes, its rows S apart, or as far as it is wide.
(def resize_where ((win Win) (ns (list int)) (s int)) Where
  (match win
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (match bf
        ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
          (if (eq (length ns) 3)
              (Where cva cn csd)
              (Where (nth ns 3) (if (ge (length ns) 5) (nth ns 4) 0) (if (eq (length ns) 6) (nth ns 5) (mul (nth ns 1) s)))))))))

; The state served, its answer sent to the request payload.
(def answered ((s (Served Wm)) (payload (list int))) Wm
  (match s ((Served v r) (let a (request_answer payload r) v))))

; The window a resize's numbers ns are of, if from is its client and the
; size fits the screen; or why not.
(def resize_checked ((v Wm) (from int) (ns (list int))) (Result Win (list int))
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws (nth ns 0))
        ((None) ((Err Win (list int)) (append "no window " (digits (nth ns 0)))))
        ((Some win)
          (if (not (eq (win_pid win) from))
              ((Err Win (list int)) "not that window's client")
              (if (if (lt (nth ns 1) 1) true (if (lt (nth ns 2) 1) true (gt (outer_w (win_deco win) (nth ns 1)) w)))
                  ((Err Win (list int)) "a window must fit the screen")
                  ((Ok Win (list int)) win))))))))

; A resize refused for why, and the window as it was: the client's new
; buffer at wh, which wm mapped, given up again, if it is a new one.
(def resize_refused ((v Wm) (win Win) (wh Where) (why (list int))) (Served Wm)
  (match wh
    ((Where va pages sd)
      (let u (if (if (eq va (win_cva win)) true (eq va (spare_va (win_spare win)))) 0 (match (shm_unmap va pages) ((ShmUnmapped) 0) ((ShmUnmapNotYours) 0) ((ShmUnmapTooMany) 0)))
        (refused v why)))))

; Where in wm a window's other buffer is, -1 for none; its pages; and
; where the display has them.
(def spare_va ((sp Spare)) int (match sp ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend) va) ((NoSpare) -1)))
(def spare_pages ((sp Spare)) int (match sp ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend) n) ((NoSpare) 0)))
(def spare_dva ((sp Spare)) int (match sp ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend) dva) ((NoSpare) 0)))

; Window win's other buffer given up, if it has one: its id forgotten by
; the display, which unmaps it, and its pages by wm: 0.
(def spare_dropped ((d Display) (win Win)) int
  (match (win_spare win)
    ((NoSpare) 0)
    ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend)
      (let f (display_forget d (win_spare_id win))
        (match (shm_unmap va n) ((ShmUnmapped) 0) ((ShmUnmapNotYours) 0) ((ShmUnmapTooMany) 0))))))

; Where in wm a window's content's buffer is, and its buffers as shared.
(def win_cva ((w Win)) int (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) cva)))
(def win_bufs ((w Win)) Bufs (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) bf)))

; The new content given to the display under the content's other bank's
; id: in the pages it has of the window's own buffer, if it is in that
; one, or of its other buffer, if it is in that, as a client that paints
; the buffer not shown resizes; else in a new one shared with it. The
; other buffer, if it is not the one, is given up first, as its id is
; the one taken. Once it has it, the request answered, the
; client asked for the next size, and the rest made.
(def resize_content ((v Wm) (win Win) (nw int) (nh int) (wh Where) (payload (list int))) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match wh
        ((Where va given sd)
          (match (win_bufs win)
            ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
              (let s (display_scale d)
                (let need (buffer_pages sd (mul nh s))
                  (let spared (eq va (spare_va sp))
                    (let pages (if (eq va (win_cva win)) cn (if spared (spare_pages sp) (max given need)))
                      (if (if (lt pages need) true (lt sd (mul nw s)))
                          (answered (resize_refused v win wh "the buffer is too small for the size") payload)
                          (let cid (win_spare_id win)
                            (let dropped (if spared 0 (spare_dropped d win))
                              (match (if (if (eq va (win_cva win)) true spared)
                                         (let at (if spared (spare_dva sp) dcva)
                                           (let e (display_buffer_at d cid (mul nw s) (mul nh s) sd at pages)
                                             (if (is_empty e) ((Ok int (list int)) at) ((Err int (list int)) e))))
                                         (display_buffer_shared d cid (mul nw s) (mul nh s) sd va pages))
                            ((Err e) (answered (resize_refused v win wh e) payload))
                            ((Ok there)
                              (let a (answered (okay v) payload)
                                (let next (resize_ask_next win nw nh)
                                  (resize_finished (resize_chrome v win nw nh (Where va pages sd) there) win nw nh next)))))))))))))))))))

; The window's client asked for the size the user has dragged it to, if
; it was asked for one and that is not nw by nh, the size it has answered
; with: whether it was.
(def resize_ask_next ((win Win) (nw int) (nh int)) bool
  (match win
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (match sz
        ((Sizing k e ww wh asking re go)
          (if (if asking (not (if (eq ww nw) (eq wh nh) false)) false)
              (let t (port_tell port (win_notice id (size_notice ww wh))) true)
              false))))))

; What making the rest of window win's resize to nw by nh came to. If it
; failed, the window is as it was, and its client, which has given up
; the buffer shown, is asked for the size shown again: unless it has
; been asked for another already, or that is the size that failed.
(def resize_finished ((s (Served Wm)) (win Win) (nw int) (nh int) (next bool)) Wm
  (match s
    ((Served v r)
      (if (not (starts_with r "error"))
          v
          (match win
            ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
              (if (if next true (if (eq nw cw) (eq nh ch) false))
                  v
                  (let t (port_tell port (win_notice id (size_notice cw ch))) v))))))))

; The chrome made for the new size and given to the display, the content
; being at wh here and there in the display: in the one it has, if its
; canvas holds it, painted where it shows, its rows where they were, which
; the screen takes up only at the restack; else in a new one, with room to
; grow. Its canvas is all of its buffer, the stride its width. A window
; its client decorates has none to make.
(def resize_chrome ((v Wm) (win Win) (nw int) (nh int) (wh Where) (there int)) (Served Wm)
  (match win
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (match bf
        ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
          (if (has_chrome dc)
              (resize_chrome_made v win nw nh wh there)
              (resize_shown v win nw nh wh there tc tva tn dtva)))))))

; resize_chrome's chrome, wm's own title bar and frame.
(def resize_chrome_made ((v Wm) (win Win) (nw int) (nh int) (wh Where) (there int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match win
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (match bf
            ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
              (let s (display_scale d)
                (let cid (win_spare_id win)
                  (let tid (chrome_id id (sub 1 (win_bank win)))
                    (let front (eq id (win_id (head ws)))
                      (let tw (mul (outer_w dc nw) s)
                        (let th (mul (chrome_h dc nh) s)
                          (if (if (le tw (canvas_w tc)) (le th (canvas_h tc)) false)
                              (let tc2 (paint_chrome tc font title nw nh front)
                                (let e (display_buffer_at d tid tw th (canvas_w tc2) dtva tn)
                                  (if (not (is_empty e))
                                      (let f (display_forget d cid) (resize_refused v win wh e))
                                      (resize_shown v win nw nh wh there tc2 tva tn dtva))))
                              (match (ui_buffer_at (grown (outer_w dc nw)) (grown (chrome_h dc nh)) s)
                                ((UiNoBuf why) (let f (display_forget d cid) (resize_refused v win wh why)))
                                ((UiBuf tva2 pages big)
                                  (let tc2 (paint_chrome big font title nw nh front)
                                    (match (display_buffer_shared d tid tw th (canvas_w tc2) tva2 pages)
                                      ((Err e) (let f (display_forget d cid) (let u (ui_buffer_free tva2 pages big) (resize_refused v win wh e))))
                                      ((Ok dtva2) (resize_shown v win nw nh wh there tc2 tva2 pages dtva2))))))))))))))))))))

; A buffer's side n with room to grow: a quarter more, and 64.
(def grown ((n int)) int (add n (add (div n 4) 64)))

; Win with its new buffers: their corners shaped, the window moved to
; where a maximize or a restore takes it, else if its left or top edge
; was dragged, and then the screen shown with them. Once no answer is
; awaited, the goal is met.
(def resize_shown ((v Wm) (win Win) (nw int) (nh int) (wh Where) (there int) (tc Canvas) (tva int) (tn int) (dtva int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match win
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title otc ocva otva obf app sz dc)
          (match sz
            ((Sizing ok edges ww wht asking re go)
              (match wh
                ((Where cva cn csd)
                  (let k (sub 1 ok)
                    (let s (shape_window d id k (sub 1 (win_cbank win)) dc nw nh)
                      (let again (if asking (not (if (eq ww nw) (eq wht nh) false)) false)
                        (let goal (not (rect_empty go))
                          (let nx (if goal (rect_x go) (if (has_edge edges (edge_left)) (add x (sub cw nw)) x))
                            (let ny (below_bar (if goal (rect_y go) (if (has_edge edges (edge_top)) (add y (sub ch nh)) y)))
                              (resize_done v win (Win id port pid nx ny nw nh 0 title tc cva tva (resized_bufs obf ocva cw ch cva cn there csd tn dtva) app
                                                      (Sizing k edges ww wht again re (if again go (rect_none))) dc)))))))))))))))))

; A window's buffers after a resize, obf before it, its content then at
; ocva in wm and cw by ch: the content now at nva, cn pages, at there in
; the display, its rows csd apart, under the content's other bank; the
; chrome's tn pages at dtva in the display. A window that has an other
; buffer keeps the content it had as that, unless the resize was in it.
(def resized_bufs ((obf Bufs) (ocva int) (cw int) (ch int) (nva int) (cn int) (there int) (csd int) (tn int) (dtva int)) Bufs
  (match obf
    ((Bufs ocn odcva ocsd otn odtva fw ck sp)
      (Bufs cn there csd tn dtva fw (sub 1 ck)
            (match sp
              ((NoSpare) (NoSpare))
              ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend) (if (eq nva ocva) (NoSpare) (Spare ocva ocn odcva ocsd cw ch false))))))))

; The window old replaced by nwin, whose new buffers were painted before
; the display had them, so it took their pixels with them: the screen
; shown with them, and the old ones forgotten by the display and given up.
(def resize_done ((v Wm) (old Win) (nwin Win)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws nwin) n ptr drag kp pp bar)
        (let e (restack v2)
          (let u (resize_old_given_up d old nwin)
            (okay v2)))))))

; The window's old ids, which a resize replaced with nwin's, forgotten by
; the display, which keeps pages a new id is over; and each old buffer
; nwin no longer uses given up. The content kept as nwin's other buffer
; keeps its id and pages.
(def resize_old_given_up ((d Display) (old Win) (nwin Win)) int
  (let k (win_bank old)
    (let id (win_id old)
      (let kept (eq (spare_va (win_spare nwin)) (win_cva old))
        (let f1 (if kept "" (display_forget d (win_content_id old)))
          (let f2 (if (has_chrome (win_deco old)) (display_forget d (chrome_id id k)) "")
            (match old
              ((Win oid port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
                (match bf
                  ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
                    (let a (if (if kept true (eq cva (win_cva nwin))) 0 (match (shm_unmap cva cn) ((ShmUnmapped) 0) ((ShmUnmapNotYours) 0) ((ShmUnmapTooMany) 0)))
                      (if (eq tva (win_tva nwin)) 0 (ui_buffer_free tva tn tc)))))))))))))

; Where in wm a window's chrome's buffer is.
(def win_tva ((w Win)) int (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) tva)))

; The windows in front before and after, told if they changed: the one
; that was, that it is not, and the one that is, that it is.
(def refocused ((before (list Win)) (after (list Win))) int
  (let b (if (is_empty before) -1 (win_id (head before)))
    (let a (if (is_empty after) -1 (win_id (head after)))
      (if (eq a b)
          0
          (let s (if (lt b 0) 0 (win_tell (head before) (focus_notice false)))
            (if (lt a 0) 0 (win_tell (head after) (focus_notice true))))))))

; Window w's client told notice, of w, as a window notice: its id first.
(def win_tell ((w Win) (notice (list int))) int (port_tell (win_port w) (told_of w notice)))

; notice as told to w's client: a window notice, w's id before it.
(def told_of ((w Win) (notice (list int))) (list int) (win_notice (win_id w) notice))

; The port wm serves on: where exit notices go. Kept nowhere, so found
; again: it is the one registered as compositor.
(def wm_port ((v Wm)) Lookup (name_lookup "compositor"))

; The screen after the window front changed: every title bar drawn as
; front or not, the layers sent, and the window's id as the reply.
(def shown_front ((v Wm) (id int)) (Served Wm)
  (let t (titles v)
    (let e (restack v)
      (if (is_empty e) (Served v (append "window " (digits id))) (refused v e)))))

(def restack ((v Wm)) (list int)
  (match v ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) (display_layers d (menu_layered (layers ws (launcher_shown (bar_launcher bar))) (menu_shown (bar_menu bar)))))))

; ls, the bar last, with the menu's card under the bar, if it is shown.
(def menu_layered ((ls (list Placed)) (shown bool)) (list Placed)
  (if (not shown)
      ls
      (let n (length ls)
        (append (take ls (sub n 1)) (cons (Placed (menu_id) (menu_x) (bar_h) 0) (drop ls (sub n 1)))))))

; Every title bar drawn, the front one active, the rest in the backdrop;
; and the top bar, with the front one's title.
(def titles ((v Wm)) int
  (match v ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) (let t (draw_titles d font ws true) (draw_bar v)))))

(def draw_titles ((d Display) (font UiFace) (ws (list Win)) (front bool)) int
  (if (is_empty ws)
      0
      (let t (draw_title d font (head ws) front)
        (draw_titles d font (tail ws) false))))

; Window w's chrome painted, in front or not, and its title bar and frame
; damaged; nothing for a window its client decorates, which draws its
; own in front or not as its focus notices say.
(def draw_title ((d Display) (font UiFace) (w Win) (front bool)) int
  (match w
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (if (not (has_chrome dc))
          0
          (let p (paint_chrome tc font title cw ch front)
            (let e (display_damage_rects d (chrome_id id (sz_bank sz)) (cons (Rect 0 0 (outer_w dc cw) (title_h)) (frame_rects cw ch))) 0))))))

; A window's chrome painted on tc, its content cw by ch: its title bar,
; then its frame under it.
(def paint_chrome ((tc Canvas) (font UiFace) (title (list int)) (cw int) (ch int) (front bool)) Canvas
  (let ow (outer_w (ServerSide) cw)
    (let p (ui_paint_nodes tc font (Rect 0 0 ow (title_h)) (title_nodes title ow front))
      (ui_paint p font (Rect 0 (title_h) ow (frame_h (ServerSide) ch)) (frame_ops cw ch front)))))

; The frame of a window, its content cw by ch, in its chrome under the
; title bar: its two sides and its foot, and its bottom corners, as far
; in as their curve, where the content's corners are cut and the frame
; shows through. The rest is under the content, and never shown.
(def frame_rects ((cw int) (ch int)) (list Rect)
  (let dc (ServerSide)
    (let r (bottom_radius dc cw ch)
      (let t (title_h)
        (let b (chrome_h dc ch)
          (cons (Rect 0 t (edge) (frame_h dc ch))
            (cons (Rect (add cw (edge)) t (edge) (frame_h dc ch))
              (cons (Rect 0 (add t ch) (outer_w dc cw) (edge))
                (cons (Rect 0 (sub b r) r r)
                  (cons (Rect (sub (outer_w dc cw) r) (sub b r) r r) (nil Rect)))))))))))

; The frame painted in its title bar's ground, in front or in the
; backdrop.
(def frame_ops ((cw int) (ch int) (front bool)) (list UiPaint)
  (ui_fills (frame_rects cw ch) (ui_headerbar_bg (ui_style) front)))

; damage ID X Y W H ..., each rectangle in its window's own rows: given
; to the display in its buffer's rows, which top turns around, all in one
; request, so they are shown together.
(def damaged ((v Wm) (ns (list int)) (acc (list Dirty))) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (if (is_empty ns)
          (let e (display_damage_many d (rev acc)) (if (is_empty e) (committed v) (refused v e)))
          (let id (nth ns 0)
            (match (find_win ws id)
              ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
              ((Some win)
                (match win
                  ((Win wid port pid wx wy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
                    (damaged v (drop_n ns 5)
                             (buffer_dirty (if (win_pending win) (win_spare_id win) (win_content_id win))
                                           (nth ns 1) (nth ns 2) (nth ns 3) (nth ns 4) top ch acc)))))))))))

; After a damage: each window whose other buffer was attached shows it
; in place of the one it showed, which becomes its other buffer, and the
; screen is shown with them, as a commit after wl_surface.attach is.
(def committed ((v Wm)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (if (any_pending ws)
          (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (swapped_all ws (nil Win)) n ptr drag kp pp bar)
            (let e (restack v2) (if (is_empty e) (okay v2) (refused v2 e))))
          (okay v)))))

; Whether any of ws has its other buffer attached.
(def any_pending ((ws (list Win))) bool
  (if (is_empty ws) false (if (win_pending (head ws)) true (any_pending (tail ws)))))

; ws, in order, each with its attached buffer shown (win_swapped).
(def swapped_all ((ws (list Win)) (acc (list Win))) (list Win)
  (if (is_empty ws) (rev acc) (swapped_all (tail ws) (cons (win_swapped (head ws)) acc))))

; w showing its other buffer, if it is attached: that its content, under
; the other bank's id, and the content it had its other buffer.
(def win_swapped ((w Win)) Win
  (match w
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (match bf
        ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
          (match sp
            ((NoSpare) w)
            ((Spare sva sn sdva ssd sw sh pend)
              (if pend
                  (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc sva tva
                       (Bufs sn sdva ssd tn dtva fw (sub 1 ck) (Spare cva cn dcva csd cw ch false)) app sz dc)
                  w))))))))

; attach ID VA N S, from from: window ID's content from now on in the
; buffer at VA here, N pages, its rows S of its own pixels apart, at the
; window's size, shown at the next damage (committed). It is given to
; the display under the content's other bank's id: as it was, if it is
; the window's other buffer already, given again only if the window's
; size has changed since; else shared anew, any other buffer given up
; first. Only the window's client may ask.
(def attach_asked ((v Wm) (from int) (id int) (va int) (pages int) (sd int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (if (not (eq (win_pid win) from))
              (refused v "not that window's client")
              (if (eq va (win_cva win))
                  (okay v)
                  (match (spare_given d win va pages sd)
                    ((Err e) (refused v e))
                    ((Ok sp) (okay (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_with_spare win sp)) n ptr drag kp pp bar)))))))))))

; w with sp as its other buffer.
(def win_with_spare ((w Win) (sp Spare)) Win
  (match w
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (match bf ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck old) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva (Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp) app sz dc))))))

; The buffer at va, pages of it, its rows sd apart, given to the display
; as win's other buffer, attached, at win's size, and shaped as its
; content; or why not.
(def spare_given ((d Display) (win Win) (va int) (pages int) (sd int)) (Result Spare (list int))
  (match win
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (let s (display_scale d)
        (let need (buffer_pages sd (mul ch s))
          (let cid (win_spare_id win)
            (if (lt sd (mul cw s))
                ((Err Spare (list int)) "the buffer is narrower than the window")
                (match (win_spare win)
                  ((Spare sva sn sdva ssd sw sh pend)
                    (if (eq va sva)
                        (if (lt sn need)
                            ((Err Spare (list int)) "the buffer is too small for the window")
                            (if (if (eq sw cw) (if (eq sh ch) (eq ssd sd) false) false)
                                ((Ok Spare (list int)) (Spare sva sn sdva sd cw ch true))
                                (let e (display_buffer_at d cid (mul cw s) (mul ch s) sd sdva sn)
                                  (if (is_empty e)
                                      (let k (shape_content d cid dc cw ch) ((Ok Spare (list int)) (Spare sva sn sdva sd cw ch true)))
                                      ((Err Spare (list int)) e)))))
                        (spare_shared d win va (max pages need) sd)))
                  ((NoSpare) (spare_shared d win va (max pages need) sd))))))))))

; The buffer at va, pages of it, its rows sd apart, new to wm, given to
; the display as win's other buffer, attached, the one it had given up
; first; or why not, its pages given up again.
(def spare_shared ((d Display) (win Win) (va int) (pages int) (sd int)) (Result Spare (list int))
  (match win
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (let s (display_scale d)
        (let cid (win_spare_id win)
          (let dr (spare_dropped d win)
            (match (display_buffer_shared d cid (mul cw s) (mul ch s) sd va pages)
              ((Err e) (let u (shm_unmap va pages) ((Err Spare (list int)) e)))
              ((Ok dva) (let k (shape_content d cid dc cw ch) ((Ok Spare (list int)) (Spare va pages dva sd cw ch true)))))))))))

; Window win's client told its other buffer is released, if the display
; says id, the other buffer's, is read no more: 0.
(def release_told ((win Win) (id int)) int
  (match (win_spare win)
    ((NoSpare) 0)
    ((Spare va n dva sd sw sh pend)
      (if (if (not pend) (eq (win_spare_id win) id) false) (win_tell win (release_notice 0)) 0))))

; Each of ws told of the release of display buffer id, if it is its.
(def releases_told ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) int
  (if (is_empty ws) 0 (let t (release_told (head ws) id) (releases_told (tail ws) id))))

; Rows y up to y + n of a ring of ch rows read from top, as its buffer's:
; one rectangle, or two where they wrap, onto acc, reversed.
(def buffer_dirty ((bid int) (x int) (y int) (dw int) (n int) (top int) (ch int) (acc (list Dirty))) (list Dirty)
  (let b0 (mod (add (mod (add y top) ch) ch) ch)
    (let k (min n ch)
      (if (le (add b0 k) ch)
          (cons (Dirty bid (Rect x b0 dw k)) acc)
          (cons (Dirty bid (Rect x 0 dw (sub k (sub ch b0)))) (cons (Dirty bid (Rect x b0 dw (sub ch b0))) acc))))))

; top ID T: the window's buffer read from row T.
(def topped ((v Wm) (id int) (top int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_top win top)) n ptr drag kp pp bar)
            (let e (restack v2) (if (is_empty e) (okay v2) (refused v2 e)))))))))

; Whether window w's client has asked to be told the next frame.
(def win_frame_wanted ((w Win)) bool
  (match w ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (match bf ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp) fw)))))

; w, its client to be told the next frame if want.
(def win_framing ((w Win) (want bool)) Win
  (match w
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (match bf ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp) (Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva (Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva want ck sp) app sz dc))))))

; frame ID, from from: the window's client told the display's next
; frame, as wl_surface.frame's done is; only the window's client may ask.
(def frame_asked ((v Wm) (from int) (id int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (if (not (eq (win_pid win) from))
              (refused v "not that window's client")
              (okay (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_framing win true)) n ptr drag kp pp bar))))))))

; ws once frame n is shown: each window whose client asked for a frame
; told it, as a window notice, and asked no more.
(def frames_told ((ws (list Win)) (n int) (acc (list Win))) (list Win)
  (if (is_empty ws)
      (rev acc)
      (let win (head ws)
        (if (win_frame_wanted win)
            (let t (win_tell win (shown_notice n)) (frames_told (tail ws) n (cons (win_framing win false) acc)))
            (frames_told (tail ws) n (cons win acc))))))

; A notice from the display, m: a frame shown, told to the windows that
; asked; a buffer released, told to the client whose window's other
; buffer it is; anything else is nothing to wm.
(def display_noticed ((v Wm) (m Message)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let f (shown_notice_at m 0)
        (if (lt f 0)
            (let r (release_notice_at m 0) (let t (if (lt r 0) 0 (releases_told ws r)) v))
            (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (frames_told ws f (nil Win)) n ptr drag kp pp bar))))))

(def retitled ((v Wm) (id int) (title (list int))) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_titled win title)) n ptr drag kp pp bar)
            (let t (titles v2) (okay v2))))))))

(def closed ((v Wm) (id int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (without_win ws id) n ptr drag kp pp bar)
        (let e (restack v2)
          (let t (if (is_empty (without_win ws id)) 0 (refocused ws (without_win ws id)))
            (let t2 (titles v2)
            (let k (match (find_win ws id) ((Some win) (win_bank win)) ((None) 0))
            (let f1 (match (find_win ws id) ((Some win) (let f0 (spare_dropped d win) (display_forget d (win_content_id win)))) ((None) ""))
              (let f2 (if (win_chromed ws id) (display_forget d (chrome_id id k)) "")
                (let u (give_up (with_id ws id) (display_scale d)) (okay v2))))))))))))

; Whether window id of ws has wm's chrome.
(def win_chromed ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) bool
  (match (find_win ws id) ((Some win) (has_chrome (win_deco win))) ((None) false)))

; The windows of ws with id: one, or none.
(def with_id ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) (list Win)
  (if (is_empty ws) ws (if (eq (win_id (head ws)) id) (cons (head ws) (nil Win)) (with_id (tail ws) id))))

; Each closed window's buffers given up, once the display has dropped
; them: the content's, which its client shared with wm, and the chrome's,
; wm's own, made at scale s, its region closed too, so wm can open
; windows for ever. Each one's memory is freed once no process maps it.
(def give_up ((ws (list Win)) (s int)) int
  (if (is_empty ws)
      0
      (match (head ws)
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (match bf
            ((Bufs cn dcva csd tn dtva fw ck sp)
              (let a (shm_unmap cva cn)
                (let b (if (has_chrome dc) (ui_buffer_free tva tn tc) 0)
                  (give_up (tail ws) s)))))))))

; Every window of pid, which has exited, closed, and what wm waited on it
; for, an answer or its first window, given up.
(def gone ((v Wm) (pid int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (close_all (with_launches v (launches_gone (bar_launches bar) pid)) (of_pid ws pid)))))

(def close_all ((v Wm) (ws (list Win))) Wm
  (if (is_empty ws) v (match (closed v (win_id (head ws))) ((Served v2 r) (close_all v2 (tail ws))))))

(def window_lines ((v Wm)) (list int)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ptr
        ((Ptr px py b over grab ac shape tc)
          (append (win_lines ws true) (append "pointer " (append (digits px) (append " " (append (digits py) (if (is_empty shape) "" (append " " shape))))))))))))

; A line of each of ws, the first in front if front: its id, title, top
; left, content's width and height, front or -, and its client's pid,
; so that two windows of one client are seen to be.
(def win_lines ((ws (list Win)) (front bool)) (list int)
  (if (is_empty ws)
      ""
      (match (head ws)
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (append (unwords (cons (digits id) (cons title (cons (digits x) (cons (digits y) (cons (digits cw) (cons (digits ch)
                    (cons (if front "front" "-") (cons (digits pid) (nil (list int)))))))))))
                  (append "\n" (win_lines (tail ws) false)))))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- desktop

; desktop CMD: drawn on the desktop, and shown.
(def drew ((v Wm) (args (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (match (ui_parse_draw args)
    ((Err why) (refused v why))
    ((Ok dc)
      (match dc
        ((UiDrawBasic cmd) (painted_desktop v cmd))
        ((UiDrawRound x y rw rh r c) (desk_shown v (wm_draw v dc)))
        ((UiDrawButton x y k label) (desk_shown v (wm_draw v dc)))
        ((UiDrawIcon x y name sc c) (desk_shown v (wm_draw v dc)))))))

; One of the toolkit's commands, done on the desktop.
(def wm_draw ((v Wm) (dc UiDraw)) Canvas
  (match v ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) (ui_draw_exec desk font dc))))

(def painted_desktop ((v Wm) (cmd Command)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match cmd
        ((CmdSize) (Served v (append "size " (append (digits w) (append " " (digits h))))))
        ((CmdFont) (Served v (append "font " (append (digits (glyph_w)) (append " " (digits (glyph_h)))))))
        ((CmdScroll dy c) (refused v "the desktop does not scroll"))
        ((CmdSplash percent)
          (match (load_wallpaper (display_scale d) percent)
            ((BgBad why) (refused v why))
            ((BgOk bg2) (desk_shown (Wm d cl w h desk font bg2 ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) (paint_background desk bg2)))))
        ((CmdRestore x y rw rh) (desk_shown v (restore_rect desk bg (rect_scaled (Rect x y rw rh) (display_scale d)))))
        ((CmdChar x y code c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_text desk font x y c -1 (cons code (nil int)))))
        ((CmdText x y fg bgc cs) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_text desk font x y fg bgc cs)))
        ((CmdLine x0 y0 x1 y1 c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_line desk x0 y0 x1 y1 c (display_scale d))))
        ((CmdCircle cx cy r c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_circle desk cx cy r c (display_scale d))))
        ((CmdDisc cx cy r c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_disc desk cx cy r c (display_scale d))))
        ((CmdRect x y rw rh c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_outline desk x y rw rh c (display_scale d))))
        ((CmdFill x y rw rh c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_fill desk (Rect x y rw rh) c (display_scale d))))
        ((CmdClear c) (desk_shown v (ui_draw_fill desk (Rect 0 0 w h) c (display_scale d))))))))

; The desktop shown again, once drawn on; its canvas is a region, so the
; one drawn on is the one v holds.
(def desk_shown ((v Wm) (drawn Canvas)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let e (display_damage d (desktop_id) (Rect 0 0 w h))
        (if (is_empty e) (okay v) (refused v e))))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- pointer

; A tablet's report: the pointer at its place, scaled to the screen.
(def pointed ((v Wm) (ev PointerEvent)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ev
        ((PointerEvent px py buttons) (pointer_at v (scaled px w) (scaled py h) buttons))))))

; A mouse's report: the wheel's turn, if it turned, where the pointer is,
; then the pointer moved by it, a pixel a count, kept on the screen.
(def nudged ((v Wm) (ev PointerMotion)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ptr
        ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc)
          (match ev
            ((PointerMotion dx dy buttons wdx wdy)
              (let v2 (if (if (eq wdx 0) (eq wdy 0) false) v (wheel_at v x y wdx wdy))
                (pointer_at v2 (clamp (add x dx) 0 (sub w 1)) (clamp (add y dy) 0 (sub h 1)) buttons)))))))))

; v from lo to hi.
(def clamp ((v int) (lo int) (hi int)) int (max lo (min v hi)))

; The pointer at x, y on the screen with buttons down: shown there, what
; it is over or dragging told, and its shape as what it is over says.
(def pointer_at ((v Wm) (x int) (y int) (buttons int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let m (display_move d x y)
        (match ptr
          ((Ptr ox oy was over grab ac shape tc)
            (pointer_shaped
              (forwarded (moved (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n (Ptr x y buttons over grab ac shape tc) drag kp pp bar)
                                x y (bit_and was 1) (bit_and buttons 1))
                         was))))))))

; The pointer shown as what it is over says, as GNOME's is: a resize
; pointer over a window's edge, or while one is dragged, the arrow
; elsewhere. Its image is painted and given to the display only when it
; changes.
(def pointer_shaped ((v Wm)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ptr
        ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc)
          (let want (pointer_wanted v x y)
            (if (eq want shape)
                v
                (let p (ui_paint_named_cursor ac font want)
                  (let e (display_cursor d (arrow_id) (ui_cursor_hot_x want (display_scale d)) (ui_cursor_hot_y want (display_scale d)))
                    (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n (Ptr x y b over grab ac want tc) drag kp pp bar))))))))))

; Which pointer x, y wants: the resize pointer of the edges being
; dragged, or of those it is over, as edges_at says; else the arrow, "".
(def pointer_wanted ((v Wm) (x int) (y int)) (list int)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match drag
        ((Resizing id e px py wx wy cw ch) (resize_cursor e))
        ((Dragging id ox oy when) "")
        ((NoDrag)
          (if (if (pointer_held v) true (on_bar y))
              ""
              (match (hit ws x y)
                ((OnEdge win e) (resize_cursor e))
                ((OnClose win) "") ((OnTitle win) "") ((OnContent win cx cy) "") ((OnFrame win) "") ((OnDesktop) ""))))))))

; The pointer for dragging edges e: across for the left or right alone,
; up and down for the top or bottom alone, and for a corner the diagonal
; it moves along.
(def resize_cursor ((e int)) (list int)
  (let across (if (has_edge e (edge_left)) true (has_edge e (edge_right)))
    (let down (if (has_edge e (edge_top)) true (has_edge e (edge_bottom)))
      (if (not down)
          (if across "ew-resize" "")
          (if (not across)
              "ns-resize"
              (if (eq (has_edge e (edge_left)) (has_edge e (edge_top))) "nwse-resize" "nesw-resize"))))))

; The pointer told to the window it is for, once wm has done what it
; does with it: the window holding it since a press in its content, or
; else the one whose content it is in; none while a title bar is dragged.
; The window it was last in is told when it has left. A press of any
; button in a window's content makes that window hold it; once no button
; is down, none does.
(def forwarded ((v Wm) (was int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ptr
        ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc)
          (let target (if (pointer_held v) ((None Win)) (pointer_target ws drag x y grab))
            (let tid (match target ((None) -1) ((Some t) (win_id t)))
              (let l (if (if (ge over 0) (not (eq over tid)) false) (told_left ws over) 0)
                (let s (match target ((None) 0) ((Some t) (win_tell t (pointer_notice (relative t x y b)))))
                  (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n (Ptr x y b tid (if (eq b 0) -1 (if (eq was 0) tid grab)) ac shape tc) drag kp pp bar))))))))))

(def pointer_target ((ws (list Win)) (drag Drag) (x int) (y int) (grab int)) (Option Win)
  (match drag
    ((Dragging id ox oy when) ((None Win)))
    ((Resizing id e px py wx wy cw ch) ((None Win)))
    ((NoDrag)
      (match (if (lt grab 0) ((None Win)) (find_win ws grab))
        ((Some w) (Some w))
        ((None) (if (on_bar y)
                    ((None Win))
                    (match (hit ws x y)
                      ((OnContent w cx cy) (Some w))
                      ((OnTitle w) ((None Win)))
                      ((OnClose w) ((None Win)))
                      ((OnFrame w) ((None Win)))
                      ((OnEdge w e) ((None Win)))
                      ((OnDesktop) ((None Win))))))))))

; Where x, y on the screen is in window w's content, with the buttons.
(def relative ((w Win) (x int) (y int) (b int)) PointerEvent
  (match w ((Win id port pid wx wy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc) (PointerEvent (sub x (add wx (border dc))) (sub y (add wy (bar_rows dc))) b))))

; The wheel turned: told to the window the pointer would be told of, with
; where the pointer is in its content. The driver sends the turn before
; the pointer event of the same report, so the place is the turn's own.
(def wheeled ((v Wm) (ev WheelEvent)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ev
        ((WheelEvent px py dx dy) (wheel_at v (scaled px w) (scaled py h) dx dy))))))

; The wheel turned dx across and dy down with the pointer at x, y on the
; screen.
(def wheel_at ((v Wm) (x int) (y int) (dx int) (dy int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (if (pointer_held v) ((None Win)) (pointer_target ws drag x y (ptr_grab ptr)))
        ((None) v)
        ((Some t) (let s (win_tell t (wheel_notice (wheel_relative t x y (WheelEvent x y dx dy)))) v))))))

(def ptr_grab ((p Ptr)) int (match p ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc) grab)))

; A wheel event with x, y on the screen made relative to w's content.
(def wheel_relative ((w Win) (x int) (y int) (ev WheelEvent)) WheelEvent
  (match ev
    ((WheelEvent ex ey dx dy)
      (match (relative w x y 0) ((PointerEvent rx ry b) (WheelEvent rx ry dx dy))))))

(def told_left ((ws (list Win)) (id int)) int
  (match (find_win ws id) ((None) 0) ((Some w) (win_tell w (leave_notice)))))

; What the left button's change, from was to now, does at x, y: the
; launcher's, while it is shown or a press on Applications holds it.
(def moved ((v Wm) (x int) (y int) (was int) (now int)) Wm
  (if (menu_busy v) (menu_moved v x y was now)
  (if (launcher_busy v) (launcher_moved v x y was now)
  (if (if (eq was 0) (eq now 1) false) (pressed v x y)
  (if (if (eq was 1) (eq now 0) false) (released v)
  (if (eq now 1) (dragged v x y false) v))))))

(def pressed ((v Wm) (x int) (y int)) Wm
  (if (on_logo_button x y)
      (with_menu_state v false (menu_logo))
      (if (on_apps_button x y)
          (with_launcher_state v false (launcher_button))
          (if (on_bar y) v (pressed_below v x y)))))

(def pressed_below ((v Wm) (x int) (y int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (hit ws x y)
        ((OnDesktop) v)
        ((OnClose win) (close_pressed v win))
        ((OnTitle win) (title_pressed v win x y))
        ((OnContent win cx cy) (raised_by v win))
        ((OnFrame win) (raised_by v win))
        ((OnEdge win e)
          (match win
            ((Win id port pid wx wy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
              (let ws2 (raised (replaced ws (win_asked win e cw ch false)) id)
                (let f (refocused ws ws2)
                  (fronted (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws2 n ptr (Resizing id e x y wx wy cw ch) kp pp bar)
                           (eq id (win_id (head ws)))))))))))))

; A press at x, y on win's title bar: win raised, and dragged, held where
; it was pressed; or, if it is the second press of a double click there,
; maximized, or restored, by the same code as maximize, and not dragged.
(def title_pressed ((v Wm) (win Win) (x int) (y int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match ptr
        ((Ptr px py b over grab ac shape tc)
          (match win
            ((Win id port pid wx wy cw ch top title tcv cva tva bf app sz dc)
              (let now (clock_ns)
                (let double (title_double tc id now)
                  (let p2 (Ptr px py b over grab ac shape (if double (TitleClick -1 0) (TitleClick id now)))
                    (let ws2 (raised ws id)
                      (let f (refocused ws ws2)
                        (let v2 (fronted (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws2 n p2 (if double (NoDrag) (Dragging id (sub x wx) (sub y wy) 0)) kp pp bar)
                                         (eq id (win_id (head ws))))
                          (if double (maximize_toggled v2 win) v2))))))))))))))

; move ID, from from: the user drags window ID by the header bar its
; client draws, as xdg_toplevel's move asks; dragged as by wm's own title
; bar from where the pointer is now, held where it holds it. Only while
; the left button is down and holds the pointer for that window, after a
; press in its content, and nothing else is dragged: else refused.
(def move_started ((v Wm) (from int) (id int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (if (not (eq (win_pid win) from))
              (refused v "not that window's client")
              (match ptr
                ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc)
                  (if (not (move_may drag b grab id))
                      (refused v "not pressed")
                      (match win
                        ((Win wid port pid wx wy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
                          (okay (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr (Dragging id (sub x wx) (sub y wy) 0) kp pp bar)))))))))))))

; edges ID E, from from: the user resizes window ID by its edges E from
; inside them, which its client draws, as xdg_toplevel's resize asks;
; resized as by the border outside it from where the pointer is now. As
; move, only while the left button is down and holds the pointer for that
; window, after a press in its content, nothing else is dragged, and E
; are edges one can drag together: else refused.
(def edges_started ((v Wm) (from int) (id int) (e int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (if (not (eq (win_pid win) from))
              (refused v "not that window's client")
              (if (not (edges_ok e))
                  (refused v (append "no edges " (digits e)))
                  (match ptr
                    ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc)
                      (if (not (move_may drag b grab id))
                          (refused v "not pressed")
                          (match win
                            ((Win wid port pid wx wy cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
                              (okay (pointer_shaped (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_asked win e cw ch false)) n ptr
                                                        (Resizing id e x y wx wy cw ch) kp pp bar)))))))))))))))

; Whether edges e can be dragged together: one side, or two that meet at
; a corner, never two that face each other.
(def edges_ok ((e int)) bool
  (if (if (lt e 1) true (gt e 15))
      false
      (let across (add (edge_left) (edge_right))
        (let down (add (edge_top) (edge_bottom))
          (not (if (eq (bit_and e across) across) true (eq (bit_and e down) down)))))))

; maximize ID, from from: window ID made to fill the screen under the
; bar, or, if it is maximized, restored to where it was and its size, as
; a double click on a header bar asks. Only the window's client may ask.
(def maximize_asked ((v Wm) (from int) (id int)) (Served Wm)
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (find_win ws id)
        ((None) (refused v (append "no window " (digits id))))
        ((Some win)
          (if (not (eq (win_pid win) from))
              (refused v "not that window's client")
              (okay (maximize_toggled v win))))))))

; v with win maximized, where and how big it is kept to restore it to, or
; restored, if it is maximized.
(def maximize_toggled ((v Wm) (win Win)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match win
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (let re (win_restore win)
            (let go (if (rect_empty re) (maximized_rect dc w h) re)
              (win_goes_to v (win_maxing win (if (rect_empty re) (Rect x y cw ch) (rect_none)) go) go))))))))

; Where a window decorated as dc goes when maximized on a screen w by h,
; and its content's size: all the screen under the top bar.
(def maximized_rect ((dc Deco) (w int) (h int)) Rect
  (Rect 0 (bar_h) (sub w (mul 2 (border dc))) (sub (sub h (bar_h)) (add (bar_rows dc) (border dc)))))

; v with win going to go: its client asked for go's size, as a drag of
; its right and bottom edges asks, the window placed at go once it
; answers (resize_shown); or, if it is that size already, moved there.
(def win_goes_to ((v Wm) (win Win) (go Rect)) Wm
  (match win
    ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
      (if (if (eq (rect_w go) cw) (eq (rect_h go) ch) false)
          (win_moved v (win_maxing win (win_restore win) (rect_none)) (rect_x go) (rect_y go))
          (resize_asked v win (add (edge_right) (edge_bottom)) (rect_w go) (rect_h go))))))

; v with win at x, y, below the bar, and the screen restacked.
(def win_moved ((v Wm) (win Win) (x int) (y int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_at win x (below_bar y))) n ptr drag kp pp bar)
        (let e (restack v2) v2)))))

; Whether a client's move or resize of window id may start: nothing
; dragged, the left button down in buttons b, and the pointer held for id.
(def move_may ((drag Drag) (b int) (grab int) (id int)) bool
  (match drag
    ((NoDrag) (if (eq (bit_and b 1) 1) (eq grab id) false))
    ((Dragging i ox oy when) false)
    ((Resizing i e px py wx wy cw ch) false)))

; A press on win's content or frame: win brought to the front.
(def raised_by ((v Wm) (win Win)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let f (refocused ws (raised ws (win_id win)))
        (fronted (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (raised ws (win_id win)) n ptr drag kp pp bar) (eq (win_id win) (win_id (head ws))))))))

; The close button pressed: the window's client asked to close it, with
; the close notice, as xdg_toplevel's close asks, and the window kept to
; be closed by force if it is still open close_wait_ns from now, on wm's
; alarm.
(def close_pressed ((v Wm) (win Win)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let s (win_tell win (close_notice))
        (let v2 (Wm d (cons (Closing (win_id win) (win_pid win) (add (clock_ns) (close_wait_ns))) cl) w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
          (let a (close_alarm v2) v2))))))

; wm's alarm set for the first close asked, or launch waited on
; (launching.l0), that is due, if one is: on the port it serves, so the
; alarm notice comes with its requests.
(def close_alarm ((v Wm)) int
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let t (launch_next (bar_launches bar) (close_next cl -1))
        (if (lt t 0)
            0
            (match (wm_port v) ((Found port) (alarm_at port t)) ((NotFound) 0)))))))

; When the first of cs is due, on clock_ns, or first if it is sooner and
; not -1; -1 for none.
(def close_next ((cs (list Closing)) (first int)) int
  (if (is_empty cs)
      first
      (match (head cs)
        ((Closing id pid t) (close_next (tail cs) (if (if (lt first 0) true (lt t first)) t first))))))

; The closes asked of cs that are due at now, and those that are not.
(data Closes (Closes (list Closing) (list Closing)))

; cs split at now into those due, onto due, and those not, onto later,
; each in its order.
(def closes_split ((cs (list Closing)) (now int) (due (list Closing)) (later (list Closing))) Closes
  (if (is_empty cs)
      (Closes (rev due) (rev later))
      (match (head cs)
        ((Closing id pid t)
          (if (le t now)
              (closes_split (tail cs) now (cons (head cs) due) later)
              (closes_split (tail cs) now due (cons (head cs) later)))))))

; wm's alarm at now: each close asked that is due ended, the client killed
; if the window is still open and still its; each launch due given up
; (launches_late); the alarm set again for the rest. port is wm's own.
(def closes_due ((v Wm) (port int) (now int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (closes_split cl now (nil Closing) (nil Closing))
        ((Closes due later)
          (let v2 (launches_late (closes_forced (Wm d later w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) due) now)
            (let a (close_alarm v2) v2)))))))

; Each of due whose window is still open, and its client's: the client
; killed. Its exit closes its windows, as any client's does. If it cannot
; be killed, a driver, or has already gone, the window is closed here.
(def closes_forced ((v Wm) (due (list Closing))) Wm
  (if (is_empty due)
      v
      (match (head due)
        ((Closing id pid t)
          (closes_forced (match (still_open (wm_wins v) id pid) ((None) v) ((Some win) (close_forced v win))) (tail due))))))

; Window id, if it is open and still pid's.
(def still_open ((ws (list Win)) (id int) (pid int)) (Option Win)
  (match (find_win ws id)
    ((None) ((None Win)))
    ((Some win) (if (eq (win_pid win) pid) (Some win) ((None Win))))))

; The windows, front first.
(def wm_wins ((v Wm)) (list Win) (match v ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) ws)))

; win's client killed, as the close button killed it before it asked:
; or, if it cannot be, the window closed here.
(def close_forced ((v Wm) (win Win)) Wm
  (match (proc_kill (win_pid win))
    ((Killed) v)
    ((KillDenied) (closed_here v win))
    ((KillNoProc) (closed_here v win))))

; end, from from: from killed, as a client asks once it has closed what
; its user closed and has nothing left to do (the toolkit, for an app
; that did nothing with a close), since a program cannot end itself but
; by returning from main. Its windows close with its exit. Refused for a
; process wm may not kill.
(def ended ((v Wm) (from int)) (Served Wm)
  (match (proc_kill from)
    ((Killed) (okay v))
    ((KillDenied) (refused v "may not end a driver"))
    ((KillNoProc) (okay v))))

; v with win closed by wm itself, its client not to be killed.
(def closed_here ((v Wm) (win Win)) Wm
  (match (closed v (win_id win)) ((Served v2 r) v2)))

; The screen after a press brought a window in front, unless it was.
(def fronted ((v Wm) (already bool)) Wm
  (if already v (let t (titles v) (let e (restack v) v))))

(def released ((v Wm)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match drag
        ((NoDrag) v)
        ((Dragging id ox oy last)
          (let v2 (dragged v (ptr_x ptr) (ptr_y ptr) true)
            (match v2 ((Wm d2 cl2 w2 h2 desk2 font2 bg2 ws2 n2 ptr2 drag2 kp2 pp2 bar2) (Wm d2 cl2 w2 h2 desk2 font2 bg2 ws2 n2 ptr2 (NoDrag) kp2 pp2 bar2)))))
        ((Resizing id e px py wx wy cw ch)
          (let v2 (dragged v (ptr_x ptr) (ptr_y ptr) true)
            (match v2 ((Wm d2 cl2 w2 h2 desk2 font2 bg2 ws2 n2 ptr2 drag2 kp2 pp2 bar2) (Wm d2 cl2 w2 h2 desk2 font2 bg2 ws2 n2 ptr2 (NoDrag) kp2 pp2 bar2)))))))))

(def ptr_x ((p Ptr)) int (match p ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc) x)))
(def ptr_y ((p Ptr)) int (match p ((Ptr x y b over grab ac shape tc) y)))

; The dragged window moved under the pointer, and the screen rebuilt if
; the last rebuild ended long enough ago, or at the drag's end. The
; rebuild's end is what is kept, not its start: a rebuild can take longer
; than drag_ns, and the moves that came in while it ran are then all
; waiting, so timing from its start would rebuild once for each of them,
; and the window would fall further behind the pointer with every one.
(def dragged ((v Wm) (x int) (y int) (last bool)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match drag
        ((NoDrag) v)
        ((Dragging id ox oy when)
          (match (find_win ws id)
            ((None) v)
            ((Some win)
              (let moved_ws (replaced ws (win_at win (sub x ox) (below_bar (sub y oy))))
                (if (if last true (ge (sub (clock_ns) when) (drag_ns)))
                    (let e (display_layers d (layers moved_ws false))
                      (Wm d cl w h desk font bg moved_ws n ptr (Dragging id ox oy (clock_ns)) kp pp bar))
                    (Wm d cl w h desk font bg moved_ws n ptr drag kp pp bar))))))
        ((Resizing id e px py wx wy cw ch)
          (match (find_win ws id)
            ((None) v)
            ((Some win)
              (match (resize_geometry (win_deco win) e (sub x px) (sub y py) wx wy cw ch w h)
                ((Size nw nh) (resize_asked v win e nw nh))))))))))

; The window win, which edges e of are being dragged to make it nw by nh,
; asked for that size, unless it is its size, or it has been asked for
; one and has not answered: it is asked again for the latest when it
; answers. The size asked for is kept.
(def resize_asked ((v Wm) (win Win) (e int) (nw int) (nh int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match win
        ((Win id port pid x y cw ch top title tc cva tva bf app sz dc)
          (match sz
            ((Sizing k oe ww wh asking re go)
              (let ask (if asking false (not (if (eq nw cw) (eq nh ch) false)))
                (let t (if ask (port_tell port (win_notice id (size_notice nw nh))) 0)
                  (Wm d cl w h desk font bg (replaced ws (win_asked win e nw nh (if asking true ask))) n ptr drag kp pp bar))))))))))

; ------------------------------------------------------------ the launcher

; The top bar, and the launcher with it.
(def wm_bar ((v Wm)) Bar (match v ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar) bar)))

; Says why on standard error, at once: wm never exits, so nothing else
; would flush it.
(def wm_says ((why (list int))) int (warn_as "wm" why))

; The launcher's page made: a buffer as wide as the screen and as high as
; what is under the bar, given to the display and painted, with the apps
; there are, and damaged, since a display that keeps a copy
; of a buffer, as the GL one does, learns of its pixels only by damage. Without it, wm goes on with no launcher.
(def with_launcher ((v Wm)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let lh (sub h (bar_h))
        (match (ui_buffer_at w lh (display_scale d))
          ((UiNoBuf why) (let s (wm_says (append "no launcher: " why)) v))
          ((UiBuf va pages c)
            (let e (give_buffer d (launcher_id) c va pages)
              (if (not (is_empty e))
                  (let s (wm_says (append "no launcher: " e)) v)
                  (let p (launcher_paint c font w lh (bar_apps bar))
                    (let dm (display_damage d (launcher_id) (Rect 0 0 w lh))
                    (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp (bar_launched bar (Launcher c false (launcher_none))))))))))))))

; Whether the launcher takes the pointer: while it is shown, and from a
; press on Applications until the button is let go.
(def launcher_busy ((v Wm)) bool
  (let l (bar_launcher (wm_bar v))
    (if (launcher_shown l) true (not (eq (launcher_pressed l) (launcher_none))))))

; The menu's card made: a buffer of the card's size, given to the display
; with its corners rounded, painted and damaged (a display that keeps a
; copy of a buffer learns of its pixels only by damage). Without it, wm
; goes on with no menu.
(def with_menu ((v Wm)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (match (ui_buffer_at (menu_w) (menu_h) (display_scale d))
        ((UiNoBuf why) (let s (wm_says (append "no menu: " why)) v))
        ((UiBuf va pages c)
          (let e (give_buffer d (menu_id) c va pages)
            (if (not (is_empty e))
                (let s (wm_says (append "no menu: " e)) v)
                (let p (menu_paint c font)
                  (let sh (display_shape d (menu_id) (ui_window_radius) (ui_window_radius) (ui_window_radius) (ui_window_radius))
                    (let dm (display_damage d (menu_id) (Rect 0 0 (menu_w) (menu_h)))
                      (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp (bar_menued bar (Menu c false (menu_none))))))))))))))

; Whether the pointer is the menu's or the launcher's, and no window's.
(def pointer_held ((v Wm)) bool
  (if (menu_busy v) true (launcher_busy v)))

; Whether the menu takes the pointer: while it is shown, and from a press
; on the logo until the button is let go.
(def menu_busy ((v Wm)) bool
  (let m (bar_menu (wm_bar v))
    (if (menu_shown m) true (not (eq (menu_pressed m) (menu_none))))))

; v with the menu shown or not, and the last press on it.
(def with_menu_state ((v Wm) (shown bool) (pressed int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp (bar_menued bar (menu_with (bar_menu bar) shown pressed))))))

; What x, y on the screen is on, to the menu.
(def menu_target_at ((x int) (y int)) int (menu_target (bar_h) x y))

; The left button's change, from was to now, at x, y, while the menu
; takes the pointer: a press is noted, and a release does what the click
; does.
(def menu_moved ((v Wm) (x int) (y int) (was int) (now int)) Wm
  (let m (bar_menu (wm_bar v))
    (if (if (eq was 0) (eq now 1) false)
        (with_menu_state v (menu_shown m) (menu_target_at x y))
        (if (if (eq was 1) (eq now 0) false)
            (menu_clicked (with_menu_state v (menu_shown m) (menu_none))
                          (menu_act (menu_pressed m) (menu_target_at x y)))
            v))))

; What a click on the menu does, as menu_act decided it.
(def menu_clicked ((v Wm) (act MenuAct)) Wm
  (match act
    ((MenuDo i) (menu_done (menu_set v false) i))
    ((MenuToggle) (menu_set (launcher_set v false) (not (menu_shown (bar_menu (wm_bar v))))))
    ((MenuClose) (menu_set v false))
    ((MenuNothing) v)))

; The menu shown, or not, and the screen and the bar made so.
(def menu_set ((v Wm) (shown bool)) Wm
  (if (eq shown (menu_shown (bar_menu (wm_bar v))))
      v
      (let v2 (with_menu_state v shown (menu_none))
        (let e (restack v2)
          (let b (draw_bar v2) v2)))))

; A key while the menu is shown: Esc pressed closes it, and every key is
; the menu's, not a window's.
(def menu_keyed ((v Wm) (k (Option KeyEvent))) Wm
  (match k
    ((None) v)
    ((Some ev)
      (match ev
        ((KeyEvent code value c mods) (if (if (eq code (ui_key_esc)) (eq value 1) false) (menu_set v false) v))))))

; Row i of the menu done: About L0S opens the About window; Shut Down
; kills pid 1, which stops the system; Restart restarts the board.
(def menu_done ((v Wm) (i int)) Wm
  (if (eq i (menu_about))
      (launch_app v (App "About" "/Applications/About.app/about" "" "") (nil (list int)))
      (if (eq i (menu_restart)) (restarted v) (shut_down v))))

; The board restarted, as sh's reboot does: nothing is told first, as
; with Shut Down. If the board cannot be, wm says why and goes on.
(def restarted ((v Wm)) Wm
  (let s (wm_says (append "cannot restart: " (board_restart))) v))

; Pid 1 killed, which stops the board: boot, as pid 1, exiting is the
; system's end. A first draft of a shutdown: nothing is told first.
(def shut_down ((v Wm)) Wm
  (match (proc_kill 1)
    ((Killed) v)
    ((KillDenied) (let s (wm_says "cannot shut down: pid 1 is a driver") v))
    ((KillNoProc) (let s (wm_says "cannot shut down: there is no pid 1") v))))

; v with the launcher shown or not, and the last press on it.
(def with_launcher_state ((v Wm) (shown bool) (pressed int)) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp (bar_launched bar (launcher_with (bar_launcher bar) shown pressed))))))

; What x, y on the screen is on, to the launcher: Applications, the rest
; of the bar, and, while it is shown, an app or its page.
(def launcher_target ((v Wm) (x int) (y int)) int
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (if (on_apps_button x y)
          (launcher_button)
          (if (on_bar y)
              (launcher_bar)
              (if (launcher_shown (bar_launcher bar))
                  (launcher_at w (length (bar_apps bar)) x (sub y (bar_h)))
                  (launcher_none)))))))

; The left button's change, from was to now, at x, y, while the launcher
; takes the pointer: a press is noted, and a release does what the click
; does.
(def launcher_moved ((v Wm) (x int) (y int) (was int) (now int)) Wm
  (let l (bar_launcher (wm_bar v))
    (if (if (eq was 0) (eq now 1) false)
        (with_launcher_state v (launcher_shown l) (launcher_target v x y))
        (if (if (eq was 1) (eq now 0) false)
            (launcher_clicked (with_launcher_state v (launcher_shown l) (launcher_none))
                              (launcher_act (launcher_pressed l) (launcher_target v x y)))
            v))))

; What a click on the launcher does, as launcher_act decided it.
(def launcher_clicked ((v Wm) (act LauncherAct)) Wm
  (match act
    ((LaunchApp i) (launched v i))
    ((LaunchToggle) (launcher_toggled v))
    ((LaunchClose) (launcher_set v false))
    ((LaunchNothing) v)))

; The launcher closed if it is shown, else opened, with the apps there
; are by then.
(def launcher_toggled ((v Wm)) Wm
  (if (launcher_shown (bar_launcher (wm_bar v)))
      (launcher_set v false)
      (launcher_set (apps_refreshed v) true)))

; v with the apps there are now, if they are not those it has: they are
; set, and the launcher painted again and damaged.
(def apps_refreshed ((v Wm)) Wm
  (match (app_refreshed (bar_apps (wm_bar v)))
    ((None) v)
    ((Some apps) (with_apps v apps))))

; v with apps in place of its own, painted on the launcher's page, if it
; has one, and the page damaged, as a display that keeps a copy of a
; buffer learns of its pixels only by damage.
(def with_apps ((v Wm) (apps (list App))) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let bar2 (bar_with_apps bar apps)
        (let lh (sub h (bar_h))
          (match (bar_launcher bar2)
            ((NoLauncher) (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar2))
            ((Launcher c shown pressed)
              (let p (launcher_paint c font w lh apps)
                (let dm (display_damage d (launcher_id) (Rect 0 0 w lh))
                  (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar2))))))))))

; The launcher shown, or not, and the screen and the bar made so.
(def launcher_set ((v Wm) (shown bool)) Wm
  (if (eq shown (launcher_shown (bar_launcher (wm_bar v))))
      v
      (let v2 (with_launcher_state v shown (launcher_none))
        (let e (restack v2)
          (let b (draw_bar v2) v2)))))

; A key while the launcher is shown: Esc pressed closes it, and every
; key is the launcher's, not a window's.
(def launcher_keyed ((v Wm) (k (Option KeyEvent))) Wm
  (match k
    ((None) v)
    ((Some ev)
      (match ev
        ((KeyEvent code value c mods) (if (if (eq code (ui_key_esc)) (eq value 1) false) (launcher_set v false) v))))))

; App i launched, once the launcher has closed, so that a window it
; opens is in front of the windows there were.
(def launched ((v Wm) (i int)) Wm
  (let v2 (launcher_set v false)
    (match (app_number (bar_apps (wm_bar v2)) i)
      ((None) v2)
      ((Some a) (launch_app v2 a (nil (list int)))))))

; App i of apps, from 0, if there is one.
(def app_number ((apps (list App)) (i int)) (Option App)
  (if (is_empty apps) ((None App)) (if (eq i 0) (Some (head apps)) (app_number (tail apps) (sub i 1)))))

; ---------------------------------------------------------- launching

; App a launched with args, the one way every launch goes (launching.l0):
; its name looked up; found, the app asked to open them; not, and the app
; starting, the launch held until it has started; else its program
; started with them. Either way the app's window comes to the front with
; the focus: the one its answer names, its front one, or its first.
(def launch_app ((v Wm) (a App) (args (list (list int)))) Wm
  (let exec (app_exec a)
    (match (launch_choice (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) exec (name_lookup (app_port_name exec)))
      ((LaunchAsk port) (launch_asked v a port args))
      ((LaunchHold) (with_launches v (launch_held (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) exec args)))
      ((LaunchStart) (launch_spawned v a args)))))

; launch NAME ARG ...: the app NAME names launched with the ARGs, as the
; launcher launches it, the launcher closed first; NAME its name as the
; launcher shows it, its bundle's or its exec (launch_named). The apps
; are read again for a name wm does not know. ok as soon as it is
; launched: the open's answer, or the app's window, comes later.
(def launch_requested ((v Wm) (args (list (list int)))) (Served Wm)
  (if (is_empty args)
      (refused v "launch takes an app")
      (match (launch_named (bar_apps (wm_bar v)) (head args))
        ((Some a) (okay (launch_app (launcher_set v false) a (tail args))))
        ((None)
          (let v2 (apps_refreshed v)
            (match (launch_named (bar_apps (wm_bar v2)) (head args))
              ((Some a) (okay (launch_app (launcher_set v2 false) a (tail args))))
              ((None) (refused v2 (append "no app " (head args))))))))))

; v waiting on ls, its alarm set for the soonest of them and its closes.
(def with_launches ((v Wm) (ls (list Launch))) Wm
  (match v
    ((Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp bar)
      (let v2 (Wm d cl w h desk font bg ws n ptr drag kp pp (bar_waiting bar ls))
        (let a (close_alarm v2) v2)))))

; The app a, running with its name at port, asked to open args, its
; answer to wm's own port, and waited on for launch_answer_ns. If it
; cannot be asked, its front window comes forward at once, and wm says
; why.
(def launch_asked ((v Wm) (a App) (port int) (args (list (list int)))) Wm
  (let pid (port_client (wm_wins v) port)
    (match (wm_port v)
      ((NotFound) v)
      ((Found me)
        (match (app_open_request me args)
          ((Err why) (let s (wm_says (append "cannot ask " (append (app_name a) (append ": " why)))) (launch_shown v 0 pid)))
          ((Ok b)
            (match (port_send_bytes port b 0 (bytes_len b))
              ((Sent) (with_launches v (append (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) (cons (LaunchAsked (app_exec a) pid port (add (clock_ns) (launch_answer_ns))) (nil Launch)))))
              ((SendNoPort) (launch_unasked v a pid (SendNoPort)))
              ((SendFull) (launch_unasked v a pid (SendFull)))
              ((SendTooBig) (launch_unasked v a pid (SendTooBig))))))))))

; App a, pid, not asked, as sending to it answered s: said, and its front
; window brought forward.
(def launch_unasked ((v Wm) (a App) (pid int) (s Sending)) Wm
  (let w (wm_says (append "cannot ask " (append (app_name a) (append " to open: " (sending_why s)))))
    (launch_shown v 0 pid)))

; The client whose windows' events go to port, the first window's, or -1
; if no window's do.
(def port_client ((ws (list Win)) (port int)) int
  (if (is_empty ws) -1 (if (eq (win_port (head ws)) port) (win_pid (head ws)) (port_client (tail ws) port))))

; App a's program started with args, or with the inittab's arguments for
; none, and waited on for its first window, launch_start_ns. Its exit is
; watched, so that its slot of the process table is free as it exits,
; which wm, its parent, never waits for; its windows close then, as any
; client's do.
(def launch_spawned ((v Wm) (a App) (args (list (list int)))) Wm
  (let s (spawn_path (app_exec a) (if (is_empty args) ((None (list (list int)))) (Some args)))
    (match s
      ((Spawned pid)
        (let wt (match (watch_client v pid) ((Watched) 0) ((WatchNoProc) 0) ((WatchFull) 0))
          (with_launches v (append (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) (cons (LaunchStarting (app_exec a) pid (add (clock_ns) (launch_start_ns)) (nil (list (list int)))) (nil Launch))))))
      ((SpawnNoEntry) (let w (wm_says (append "cannot start " (append (app_name a) (append ": no program " (app_exec a))))) v))
      ((SpawnNotProgram) (let w (cannot_launch a s) v))
      ((SpawnTooBig) (let w (cannot_launch a s) v))
      ((SpawnNoRoom) (let w (cannot_launch a s) v)))))

; Says why app a did not start, as spawning it answered s.
(def cannot_launch ((a App) (s Spawn)) int
  (wm_says (append "cannot start " (append (app_name a) (append ": " (spawn_why s))))))

; The window id of pid brought to the front with the focus, as a press on
; it brings it; for id 0, or one that is not open or not pid's, pid's
; front window; nothing if pid has none.
(def launch_shown ((v Wm) (id int) (pid int)) Wm
  (match (launch_window (wm_wins v) id pid)
    ((None) v)
    ((Some win) (raised_by v win))))

; The window launch_shown brings forward, of ws, if there is one.
(def launch_window ((ws (list Win)) (id int) (pid int)) (Option Win)
  (match (if (gt id 0) (still_open ws id pid) ((None Win)))
    ((Some win) (Some win))
    ((None) (let mine (of_pid ws pid) (if (is_empty mine) ((None Win)) (Some (head mine)))))))

; shown ID, from from, the answer to an open wm asked: the window it
; names, or from's front one, brought forward; nothing if wm asked
; nothing it answers, as one that came after its time.
(def launch_answer ((v Wm) (from int) (id int)) Wm
  (match (launch_answered (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) from)
    ((LaunchNone) v)
    ((LaunchTook l rest) (launch_shown (with_launches v rest) id from))))

; from's window opened: if from is an app wm started, it has registered
; its name, as the toolkit does before its first window, so each launch
; held meanwhile is launched again, and asks it. The window opened in
; front already.
(def launch_window_came ((v Wm) (from int)) Wm
  (match (launch_started (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) from)
    ((LaunchNone) v)
    ((LaunchTook l rest)
      (match l
        ((LaunchAsked e p port t) (with_launches v rest))
        ((LaunchStarting e p t held) (launches_again (with_launches v rest) e held))))))

; Each of held, the arguments of a launch of the app whose program is
; exec, launched again, in order: an app wm knows, or one of that
; program, named by it.
(def launches_again ((v Wm) (exec (list int)) (held (list (list (list int))))) Wm
  (if (is_empty held)
      v
      (launches_again (launch_app v (launch_app_of (bar_apps (wm_bar v)) exec) (head held)) exec (tail held))))

; The app among apps whose program is exec, or one made of exec alone.
(def launch_app_of ((apps (list App)) (exec (list int))) App
  (match (app_for_exec apps exec)
    ((Some a) a)
    ((None) (App (app_open_base exec) exec "" ""))))

; wm's alarm at now for its launches: each open unanswered in its time
; given up, the app's front window brought forward all the same, and
; said once; each start that opened no window in its time given up,
; said, and its held launches sent to it if it has its name by now, or
; dropped, so that an app slow to start is not started again for them.
(def launches_late ((v Wm) (now int)) Wm
  (match (launches_due (bar_launches (wm_bar v)) now)
    ((LaunchesDue due later) (launches_given_up (with_launches v later) due))))

; Each of due given up, in order.
(def launches_given_up ((v Wm) (due (list Launch))) Wm
  (if (is_empty due)
      v
      (let s (wm_says (launch_late_line (head due)))
        (launches_given_up
          (match (head due)
            ((LaunchAsked e pid port t) (launch_shown v 0 (if (lt pid 0) (port_client (wm_wins v) port) pid)))
            ((LaunchStarting e pid t held)
              (match (name_lookup (app_port_name e)) ((Found port) (launches_again v e held)) ((NotFound) v))))
          (tail due)))))
